{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01BdALRJihrE1xF8TaTPwytv","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now I have full context. Let me generate the worst-tier predictions for the D095 cross-architecture upgrade scenario.\n\n```yaml\ntier: worst\nnarrative_guidance: >\n  跨架构证据被质疑为不充分或 trivial。Reviewer 论证 R² exit collapse 是 decoder-only 架构的通用表征压缩\n  而非 VLA-specific effect（\"any supervised fine-tuning on decoder-only LLM would produce similar exit-layer\n  information loss\"）。OpenVLA Spatial 无明显 exit collapse（RUNNING 实验结果弱），矩阵空洞（NORA Object/Long\n  缺失）使 \"architecture-independent\" claim 站不住。D090 的 base-model-dependent 发现被解读为 \"contribution\n  只剩 exit collapse 一个 training-induced effect，太薄\"。三层级梯度仅 1 个 Tier-2 数据点（OpenVLA OXE），\n  被驳为 post-hoc narrative。Behavioral validation 完全缺失在 CoRL（robotics venue）被视为 near-fatal。\n  Reframe 方向：从 \"architecture-independent routing signature\" 转为 \"systematic diagnostic framework\n  for VLA internal representations\"。C1 (framework) 升为主要贡献，R² collapse 和 CF sensitivity\n  降为 \"findings the framework reveals\"。增加 per-layer information flow entropy、cross-task transfer\n  analysis 等 framework demonstration analyses 增强贡献厚度。\n\nimagined_experiments:\n  - name: \"SigLIP+Projector RSA vs Full VLA vs DINO\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_001\"\n    description: \"SigLIP+Projector RSA 对比 Full VLA 和 DINO，证明 action-relevant 结构源自 frozen vision encoder\"\n    expected_results:\n      siglip_projector_rsa: 0.615\n      trained_with_inst_rsa: 0.488\n      untrained_with_inst_rsa: 0.485\n      dino_rsa: 0.388\n      llm_degradation_delta: 0.127\n    result_rationale: >\n      数据已完成不变。但在 worst D095 下，此实验仅覆盖 OpenVLA 一种架构。Reviewer 攻击：\n      \"SigLIP+DinoSigLIP projector 的 RSA=0.615 是 OpenVLA-specific 的 frozen encoder 观察。\n      TracVLA 用 Phi-3-Vision 的不同 encoder，NORA 用 InternViT——你们没测这些 encoder 的 RSA。\n      单架构 encoder analysis 不能 claim architecture-independent。\" 在 framework reframe 下，\n      此实验降为 \"framework 在 OpenVLA 上的 case study\"，不再是 core contribution。\n      LLM degradation（0.615→0.488）本身仍有价值但被限定为 \"observed in Llama-2-7B backbone\"。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"SigLIP RSA Scope Limitation (Worst-Tier)\"\n        columns: [\"Source\", \"RSA\", \"Architecture Coverage\", \"Worst Interpretation\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"SigLIP+Proj\", \"0.615\", \"OpenVLA only\", \"Cannot generalize to other VLA encoders\"]\n          - [\"VLA trained\", \"0.488\", \"OpenVLA only\", \"Llama-2 specific LLM degradation\"]\n          - [\"VLA untrained\", \"0.485\", \"OpenVLA only\", \"Random-init Llama-2 specific\"]\n          - [\"DINO\", \"0.388\", \"Standalone\", \"Reference baseline, unaffected\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Bar chart 标注 'OpenVLA only' 在每个 bar 上方，突显 single-arch limitation\"\n    analysis: >\n      Framework reframe 下此实验从 C1 core evidence 降为 Section 4.1 case study。\n      价值在于 demonstrate framework 的 encoder-LLM decomposition 能力，而非 claim 本身。\n      Reviewer 不会因此给分但也不会因此扣分——neutral contribution in worst tier。\n\n  - name: \"DINO baseline RSA\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_002\"\n    description: \"Standalone vision model 参照基线\"\n    expected_results:\n      dino_rsa: 0.388\n      dino_action_R2: 0.687\n      dino_subtask_auc: 0.972\n    result_rationale: >\n      数据不变。Worst 档下 DINO 的角色不变——纯视觉 baseline。但 reviewer 可能用 DINO\n      的高 action R²=0.687 攻击论文：\"DINO（self-supervised, 无 language, 无 action training）\n      的 action probe R² 已 0.687，你们声称的 VLA training-induced R² exit collapse\n      只是从 0.68 掉到 0.60——这可能只是 fine-tuning 过程中正常的 representation compression，\n      任何 supervised fine-tuning 都会导致 exit layer 表征质量下降。\"\n    tables: []\n    figures_description:\n      - \"DINO 作为 'no-training baseline' 的 R²=0.687 标注在所有 cross-arch R² exit collapse 图上，质疑 collapse 的意义\"\n    analysis: >\n      DINO baseline 在 worst tier 被 reviewer 用来论证 exit collapse 的 trivial nature：\n      如果未训练模型 R²=0.687 而训练后 exit R² 下降到 0.55-0.60，这可能只是 supervised\n      learning 的通用 representation bottleneck 而非 VLA-specific routing。\n\n  - name: \"Per-layer RSA degradation curve\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_003\"\n    description: \"追踪 RSA 从 projector output 到 LLM 各层的变换轨迹\"\n    expected_results:\n      proj_rsa: 0.615\n      trained_peak_rsa: 0.488\n      trained_peak_layer: 9\n      untrained_peak_rsa: 0.485\n      untrained_peak_layer: 12\n      proj_to_l1_drop: 0.13\n      inverted_u_pattern: true\n    result_rationale: >\n      数据不变。Worst D095 下，inverted-U pattern 只在 OpenVLA (Llama-2) 上验证。\n      TracVLA 和 NORA 的 RSA per-layer curve 未做（只做了 R² probe），所以 \"inverted-U\n      is architecture-independent\" 无法 claim。Reviewer：\"RSA inverted-U 可能是 Llama-2\n      的 32 层架构特有的——Phi-3-mini 同为 32 层但 tokenization 不同，Qwen2.5-VL 是 36 层\n      且 GQA 架构，per-layer dynamics 可能完全不同。\" 此外 CKA 反转（plan_009）使\n      RSA 本身作为 metric 的 authority 被削弱。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"RSA Inverted-U Architecture Coverage\"\n        columns: [\"Architecture\", \"RSA Per-Layer Done?\", \"Pattern\", \"Worst Interpretation\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"OpenVLA (Llama-2-7B)\", \"Yes\", \"Inverted-U\", \"Only confirmed case\"]\n          - [\"TracVLA (Phi-3-mini)\", \"No\", \"Unknown\", \"Cannot claim generalization\"]\n          - [\"NORA (Qwen2.5-VL-3B)\", \"No\", \"Unknown\", \"Cannot claim generalization\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Per-layer RSA curve 只有 OpenVLA 一条线，旁边标 '?' 表示其他架构未验证\"\n    analysis: >\n      Framework reframe 下，inverted-U 成为 \"framework 在 OpenVLA 上发现的 pattern\" 而非\n      \"architecture-independent finding\"。可以保留为 case study 但不能 claim generality。\n      补救路径：增加 TracVLA/NORA 的 per-layer RSA 分析作为 framework demonstration。\n\n  - name: \"Output head analysis\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_004\"\n    description: \"SigLIP+projector frozen 确认, LLM 权重变化不传导到表征\"\n    expected_results:\n      vision_projector_cos_sim: 1.0\n      llm_rel_change_range: [1.22, 1.37]\n      head_vs_llm_ratio: 1.12\n      shallow_adaptation_gate: \"FAIL\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      数据不变。Worst D095 下，此实验对 framework 贡献有价值——它证明 framework 能\n      区分 frozen 和 trainable 组件。但 reviewer 可能指出：\"这是 trivial verification——\n      OpenVLA 的训练代码明确 freeze 了 vision encoder，你们只是验证了代码做了它说的事。\n      这不是 experimental finding，是 implementation confirmation。\" 在 framework paper 中，\n      这降为 Section 3 的 methodology validation paragraph，不占独立篇幅。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      Worst tier 下此实验贡献接近零——reviewer 视为 trivial。但在 framework reframe 下\n      可以包装为 \"framework 的 component attribution 能力 demonstration\"：展示 framework\n      如何分离 encoder/projector/LLM 各组件的贡献。贡献在方法论而非 finding。\n\n  - name: \"6 probing methods × 2 benchmarks 系统验证\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_005\"\n    description: \"系统性验证 trained ≈ untrained 表征结构\"\n    expected_results:\n      trained_vs_untrained_delta: 0.003\n      all_methods_consistent: true\n      cross_benchmark_replicated: true\n    result_rationale: >\n      Orphaned 但子实验完成。Worst D095 下，trained ≈ untrained 的 RSA 结论仍成立\n      但意义被 D090 reinterpret：Reviewer 说 \"trained ≈ untrained 在 distributed\n      representation (RSA/R²) 上不奇怪——frozen encoder 输出相同 L0 features，LLM\n      的 fine-tuning 主要影响 exit layer action head，中间层表征 naturally preserved。\n      这是 transfer learning 的常识，不需要 6 种方法来验证。\" 在 framework paper 中，\n      6 methods consistency 仍是 methodology 亮点——展示 framework 的 multi-method\n      triangulation 能力。但 finding 本身被视为 expected。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"6 Methods Consistency (Worst-Tier Reinterpretation)\"\n        columns: [\"Method\", \"Trained-Untrained Delta\", \"Reviewer Interpretation\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"RSA\", \"0.003\", \"Expected: frozen encoder dominates\"]\n          - [\"R² probe\", \"0.015\", \"Expected: similar L0 inputs\"]\n          - [\"CKA\", \"-0.006\", \"Reversal: undermines RSA conclusion\"]\n          - [\"Action probe\", \"0.045\", \"Marginal: routing exists but small\"]\n          - [\"Delta probe\", \"0.011\", \"Expected: similar input structure\"]\n          - [\"Classification\", \"0.001\", \"Trivially easy for both\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"6-method radar chart 显示 consistency，但加标注 'Expected under frozen encoder'\"\n    analysis: >\n      Worst tier 下 6 methods consistency 从 \"strong evidence for Claim 3\" 降为\n      \"thorough but unsurprising verification\"。Framework reframe 下，价值在于\n      demonstrate framework 的 multi-method coverage 而非 finding novelty。\n\n  - name: \"Instruction ablation\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_006\"\n    description: \"去掉 instruction text 测 RSA 变化\"\n    expected_results:\n      delta_with_vs_no_inst: 0.004\n      gate_judgment: \"FAIL — instruction 无影响 on RSA\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      数据不变。Worst D095 下，instruction 对 RSA 无影响是 OpenVLA-specific 观察。\n      Reviewer：\"RSA 测量 image token 的几何结构，当然不受 instruction 影响——image tokens\n      在 causal mask 下看不到 instruction tokens，这在你们 C1 里已经承认是 structural\n      guarantee。所以 Δ=0.004 不是 finding，是 sanity check。\" 更严重的是，TracVLA\n      和 NORA 上未做此 ablation，所以即使从 framework demonstration 角度也只是单架构。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      Worst tier 下从 \"Claim 3 evidence\" 降为 \"expected sanity check\"。\n      但在 framework paper 中，instruction ablation 仍可作为 framework 的\n      \"controlled manipulation\" capability demonstration，只是不能 claim novelty。\n\n  - name: \"2×2 matrix (training × instruction)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_007\"\n    description: \"四条件全收敛验证\"\n    expected_results:\n      four_cell_range: [0.48, 0.49]\n      bootstrap_ci_includes_0: true\n      training_effect: 0.003\n      instruction_effect: 0.004\n    result_rationale: >\n      数据不变。Worst D095 下 2×2 矩阵仍是 clean experimental design 但\n      被视为 \"confirms the obvious\"。Reviewer：\"frozen encoder + causal mask\n      已经预测了这个 null result。你的 2×2 design 很好但发现的是 expected outcome——\n      这不是 contribution，是 verification。\" 在 framework paper 中，2×2 factorial\n      design 可以作为 framework reusability 的 exemplar（\"researchers can apply\n      this factorial approach to any VLA\"），但 the finding itself 不计分。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"2×2 Matrix (Worst-Tier: Expected Null)\"\n        columns: [\"Condition\", \"RSA\", \"Reviewer Verdict\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Trained + Inst\", \"0.488\", \"Expected: frozen encoder dominates\"]\n          - [\"Trained - Inst\", \"0.489\", \"Expected: image RSA independent of text\"]\n          - [\"Untrained + Inst\", \"0.485\", \"Expected: same encoder, same RSA\"]\n          - [\"Untrained - Inst\", \"0.480\", \"Expected: null result confirmed\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"2×2 heatmap 标注 'Expected null result under frozen encoder hypothesis'\"\n    analysis: >\n      Framework paper reframe 下，2×2 matrix 的价值从 \"empirical finding\" 转为\n      \"exemplar of framework's factorial design capability\"。论文可以说\n      \"our framework enables systematic 2×2 factorial decomposition of training\n      and instruction effects\"——贡献在方法论可复用性而非结果。\n\n  - name: \"Random instruction control\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_008\"\n    description: \"随机/无意义 instruction 替代验证 RSA 不受 instruction content 影响\"\n    expected_results:\n      normal_rsa: 0.489\n      random_rsa: 0.484\n      shuffled_rsa: 0.483\n      empty_rsa: 0.472\n      max_absolute_delta: 0.017\n      instruction_invariant: true\n    result_rationale: >\n      数据不变。与 plan_006/007 相同逻辑——causal mask 使 image token RSA\n      对 instruction 天然不变。四种 instruction 条件下 Δ<0.02 是 expected 而非 surprising。\n      Worst D095 的关键攻击面不在此实验本身，而在于论文用了三个 plan（006/007/008）\n      来验证一个 structurally guaranteed result，reviewer 会认为 \"过度验证 trivial\n      prediction，浪费篇幅\"。在 8 页限制下这 3 个实验应压缩为 1 段。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      Framework reframe 下，random instruction control 与 006/007 合并为\n      \"three-way invariance verification\" 单段，作为 framework sanity check\n      的示范。占 0.5 段而非独立 subsection。\n\n  - name: \"CKA verification\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_009\"\n    description: \"CKA 指标验证 RSA 发现的 metric robustness\"\n    expected_results:\n      cka_ordering: \"untrained > trained > projector > DINO (反转 RSA)\"\n      rsa_cka_dissociation: true\n      linear_cka_last_preaction: 0.127\n    result_rationale: >\n      数据不变。Worst D095 下 CKA-RSA dissociation 变得更致命。Reviewer：\n      \"你们声称 R² exit collapse 是 architecture-independent training effect，\n      但 CKA（另一种 representational similarity metric）显示 untrained > trained——\n      即训练反而增强了 global structure。如果换个 metric 就得到相反结论，\n      那 R² exit collapse 可能只是 metric artifact 而非 genuine information loss。\n      你们怎么证明 R² 比 CKA 更能捕捉 'action-relevant information'？\"\n      在 framework paper 中，metric dissociation 可以包装为 \"framework reveals\n      metric-dependent conclusions\"——但这削弱了所有 quantitative findings 的\n      authority，因为 reviewer 会质疑每个 metric 的选择。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Metric Ordering Reversal (Worst: Authority Crisis)\"\n        columns: [\"Metric\", \"Ordering\", \"Implication\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"RSA (geometric)\", \"SigLIP > T > U > DINO\", \"Training degrades geometry\"]\n          - [\"CKA (global)\", \"U > T > SigLIP > DINO\", \"Training preserves/improves structure\"]\n          - [\"R² (functional)\", \"T_readout > DINO ≈ Proj > T_img\", \"Training enables routing\"]\n          - [\"Reviewer question\", \"—\", \"Which metric is 'correct' for VLA evaluation?\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Triple ordering diagram 标注 '?' 在每条 ordering line 上——哪个 metric 才对？\"\n    analysis: >\n      Worst tier 下 CKA dissociation 是双刃剑。Framework reframe 可以用它\n      作为 \"why we need multi-metric frameworks\"（方法论贡献），但这同时\n      undermine 了 R² exit collapse 作为 \"the architecture-independent signature\"\n      的 clean narrative。如果 exit collapse 只在 R² 下明显而 CKA 下不成立，\n      reviewer 会要求 \"architecture-independent claim 必须 metric-independent\"。\n\n  - name: \"LIBERO-Spatial cross-benchmark 扩展\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_010\"\n    description: \"第三个 benchmark（LIBERO-Spatial）交叉验证\"\n    expected_results:\n      trained_image_mean_peak_R2: 0.696\n      trained_last_preaction_peak_R2: 0.675\n      untrained_image_mean_peak_R2: 0.673\n      untrained_last_preaction_peak_R2: 0.635\n      trained_exit_R2_delta: 0.04\n      bootstrap_significance_p: 0.001\n      cross_benchmark_consistency: \"partial\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      LIBERO-Spatial 数据已部分完成（plan_010 status=preparing 但 registry 有结果）。\n      Worst D095 下，此实验是 OpenVLA 的 within-architecture cross-benchmark，\n      不是 cross-architecture validation。Reviewer：\"你从 LIBERO-Goal 换到 LIBERO-Spatial\n      只是换了 task suite 而非换了 VLA 架构——这不解决 RC4 的核心问题。\"\n      更关键的是，Spatial 的 exit R² delta 只有 0.04（vs Goal 的 0.069），\n      说明 exit collapse strength 是 task-dependent 的。Worst 解读：\n      exit collapse 不是 fundamental property 而是 task difficulty proxy——\n      harder tasks (Spatial) 产生较弱 collapse 因为模型需要保留更多 exit-layer\n      information 来处理复杂空间推理。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Cross-Benchmark Exit Collapse Comparison\"\n        columns: [\"Benchmark\", \"Trained Exit Delta\", \"Untrained Exit Delta\", \"Training Effect\", \"Interpretation\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"LIBERO-Goal\", \"0.069\", \"0.015\", \"4.6x\", \"Moderate collapse\"]\n          - [\"LIBERO-Spatial\", \"0.040\", \"0.023\", \"1.7x\", \"Weak collapse, task-dependent\"]\n          - [\"LIBERO-Object\", \"0.121\", \"0.076\", \"1.6x\", \"Moderate but untrained also collapses\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Paired bar chart: Goal vs Spatial exit delta，显示 collapse 强度的 task dependency\"\n    analysis: >\n      Cross-benchmark 结果在 worst tier 下被解读为 exit collapse 是\n      task-complexity-dependent 而非 architectural invariant。如果 collapse\n      强度随任务变化，它更像是 training-specific adaptation 而非\n      fundamental routing reorganization。Framework reframe 可以 claim\n      \"our framework reveals task-dependent routing intensity\"——\n      但这削弱了 \"architecture-independent signature\" 的 universality。\n\n  - name: \"Full-layer R² scan\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_011\"\n    description: \"33 layers × 2 conditions × 2 aggregations = 132 probes 的 R² 全层扫描\"\n    expected_results:\n      trained_image_mean_peak: {layer: 8, R2: 0.655}\n      trained_last_preaction_peak: {layer: 13, R2: 0.678}\n      untrained_image_mean_peak: {layer: 0, R2: 0.640}\n      untrained_last_preaction_peak: {layer: 32, R2: 0.609}\n      trained_exit_R2: 0.422\n      untrained_exit_R2: 0.545\n      exit_collapse_delta: 0.123\n      best_vs_best_lastpre_delta: 0.069\n      best_vs_best_lastpre_p: 0.0001\n    result_rationale: >\n      数据不变（OpenVLA 单架构）。这是 R² exit collapse 的源头证据。\n      Worst D095 下的核心攻击：Reviewer A 论证 \"exit collapse 是 decoder-only\n      LLM 在 supervised fine-tuning 下的通用行为——last preaction token 在\n      exit layer 被 action head 'consume'，functional information 被转化为\n      action prediction 而非保留在 hidden state 中。这不是 VLA-specific routing，\n      而是任何 decoder-only model 做 seq2seq mapping 时的 normal information\n      bottleneck。你需要对比 LLM 在 NLP task fine-tuning 下的 exit layer R²\n      来排除这个 confound——但你没做这个 control。\"\n      Reviewer B 补充：\"untrained model（random init）的 last_preaction R²\n      在 L10-L13 pathological (≈0) 不是 exit collapse 的对照——random init\n      model 在深层的 R²≈0 只是说明随机权重不能解码信息，这与 trained model\n      的 exit collapse 机制完全不同。你实际上没有一个 clean baseline。\"\n    tables:\n      - title: \"R² Exit Collapse: Missing Control (Worst-Tier)\"\n        columns: [\"Condition\", \"Peak R²\", \"Exit R²\", \"Delta\", \"Reviewer Critique\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Trained\", \"0.678 (L13)\", \"0.422 (L32)\", \"0.256\", \"Could be generic fine-tuning bottleneck\"]\n          - [\"Untrained (random)\", \"0.609 (L32)\", \"n/a\", \"n/a\", \"Not a valid control for collapse\"]\n          - [\"Llama-2 base\", \"0.645 (L9)\", \"0.555 (L32)\", \"0.090\", \"Base LLM also shows mild decline\"]\n          - [\"NLP fine-tuned LLM\", \"???\", \"???\", \"???\", \"Missing: the critical control\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Per-layer R² curve 添加 'NLP fine-tuning control needed' 标注在 gap 区域\"\n    analysis: >\n      Worst tier 下 exit collapse 的 VLA-specificity 被根本性质疑。\n      缺少 NLP fine-tuned LLM 的 per-layer R² control 是最大 gap——\n      如果 Llama-2 fine-tuned on any supervised task 也显示类似 exit collapse，\n      那 VLA training 的 \"unique\" contribution 归零。Framework reframe 下，\n      collapse 降为 \"one of the patterns our framework detects\"，\n      VLA-specificity claim 移除，改为 \"future work: compare across fine-tuning domains\"。\n\n  - name: \"CLIP-ViT pretraining control\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_012\"\n    description: \"CLIP ViT-L 替代 SigLIP 区分 VL pretraining vs encoder quality\"\n    expected_results:\n      clip_rsa: 0.557\n      clip_R2: 0.587\n      clip_lt_dino_in_both: true\n      vl_pretraining_not_sufficient: true\n    result_rationale: >\n      数据已完成：CLIP RSA=0.557 < DINO cls=0.692，R²=0.587 < DINO R²=0.634。\n      VL pretraining 不优于 self-supervised。Worst D095 下，此结果被 reviewer\n      进一步延伸：\"你们的 CLIP < DINO 结果说明 vision encoder 质量不取决于\n      language supervision，那你们为什么还在论文里花大量篇幅讨论 instruction\n      routing？如果最好的 action representation 来自无 language 的 DINO，\n      那 VLA 的 instruction routing 可能是 overhead 而非 feature。\"\n      这挑战了整篇论文的前提——studying instruction routing in VLA 的意义。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Encoder Comparison: DINO Dominance Problem\"\n        columns: [\"Encoder\", \"RSA\", \"R²\", \"Has Language?\", \"Worst Implication\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"DINO cls\", \"0.692\", \"0.634\", \"No\", \"Best in both metrics without language\"]\n          - [\"SigLIP+Proj\", \"0.615\", \"0.630\", \"Yes\", \"VL pretraining inferior to DINO\"]\n          - [\"CLIP ViT-L\", \"0.557\", \"0.587\", \"Yes\", \"VL pretraining worst of three\"]\n          - [\"Implication\", \"—\", \"—\", \"—\", \"Language supervision hurts encoder quality?\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Scatter plot: RSA vs R² 显示 DINO 独占右上角，两个 VL encoders 均在左下\"\n    analysis: >\n      CLIP 结果在 worst tier 下不仅否定 VL pretraining 的 encoder quality claim，\n      更挑战论文研究 instruction routing 的 motivation：如果最好的 action\n      representations 来自无 language 的 encoder，instruction routing research\n      的 practical relevance 是什么？Framework reframe 可以 acknowledge 这个\n      tension 并 argue \"understanding routing is important precisely because\n      the relationship between language and action is non-obvious\"。\n\n  - name: \"Branch-split RSA\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_013\"\n    description: \"DinoSigLIP fused backbone 中 DINOv2 vs SigLIP branch 分离\"\n    expected_results:\n      dinov2_branch_rsa: 0.619\n      siglip_branch_rsa: 0.621\n      fused_rsa: 0.634\n      post_projector_rsa: 0.615\n    result_rationale: >\n      数据不变。DINOv2 ≈ SigLIP（Δ<0.002）在 fused backbone 内。\n      Worst D095 下，此实验仅适用于 OpenVLA 的 DinoSigLIP backbone。\n      TracVLA 用 Phi-3-Vision 的不同 vision encoder（SigLIP-based 但\n      架构不同），NORA 用 InternViT。Branch-split analysis 不可迁移到\n      其他架构。Reviewer：\"这是一个 OpenVLA architecture-specific 的\n      interesting detail，但对 cross-architecture story 无贡献。\"\n      在 8 页限制下，worst tier 建议移到 appendix。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      Framework reframe 下可保留为 appendix 的 \"framework depth demo\"——\n      展示 framework 能做 sub-encoder-level 分析。但不占 main text 篇幅。\n\n  - name: \"Cross-Architecture R² Exit Collapse Matrix\"\n    plan_id: \"cross_arch_r2_matrix\"\n    description: \"3 架构 × 4 suite 的 R² exit collapse 矩阵——D095 升级的核心证据\"\n    expected_results:\n      total_matrix_cells: 10\n      cells_with_clear_collapse: 6\n      cells_with_weak_or_absent_collapse: 4\n      openvla_goal_trained_delta: 0.069\n      openvla_spatial_trained_delta: 0.04\n      openvla_object_trained_delta: 0.121\n      openvla_long_trained_delta: 0.004\n      tracvla_goal_trained_delta: 0.09\n      tracvla_spatial_trained_delta: 0.138\n      tracvla_object_trained_delta: 0.294\n      tracvla_long_trained_delta: 0.198\n      nora_goal_trained_delta: 0.691\n      nora_spatial_trained_delta: 0.302\n      mean_trained_exit_delta: 0.096\n      cross_arch_r2_peak_layer_std: 6.2\n      r2_collapse_confirmed_cells: 6\n    result_rationale: >\n      Worst tier 假设：(1) OpenVLA Spatial（RUNNING）结果弱——exit delta 仅 0.04，\n      远低于其他 cells，且 untrained 也有 0.023 delta，training effect 仅 1.7x。\n      (2) OpenVLA Long (OFT) delta=0.004 已是 outlier。(3) NORA Object/Long 缺失（无\n      checkpoint），矩阵只有 10/12 cells。(4) 6/10 cells 有 clear collapse（delta>0.10\n      且 trained>>untrained），但 4 cells 弱或例外。\n\n      Reviewer 攻击：\"你们声称 'architecture-independent' 但 10 个 cell 中 4 个\n      不支持。OpenVLA 的 2/4 suites 要么 delta≈0 (Long) 要么 delta 很小 (Spatial)。\n      只有 TracVLA 和 NORA 显示强 collapse——但这两个是你们自己训练的 checkpoint\n      而非社区标准模型。OpenVLA 是唯一的社区 checkpoint，它的结果最弱。\n      这可能说明 strong exit collapse 是你们训练流程的 artifact 而非\n      VLA training 的 inherent property。\"\n\n      Reviewer B 补充：\"NORA goal delta=0.691 和 spatial delta=0.302 是极端值——\n      比其他架构高一个数量级。这种 high variance across architectures（std=6.2\n      in peak layer）说明 exit collapse 的 magnitude 高度 architecture-dependent，\n      而你们只是 cherry-pick 了所有 delta>0 的 cell 来 claim 'consistent'。\n      Consistent direction（都 >0）但 inconsistent magnitude（0.004 到 0.691）\n      ——这不叫 architecture-independent signature，这叫 noisy observation。\"\n    tables:\n      - title: \"R² Exit Collapse Matrix (Worst-Tier Interpretation)\"\n        columns: [\"Architecture\", \"Suite\", \"Trained Delta\", \"Untrained Delta\", \"Ratio\", \"Verdict\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"OpenVLA\", \"Goal\", \"0.069\", \"0.015\", \"4.6x\", \"Moderate\"]\n          - [\"OpenVLA\", \"Spatial\", \"0.040\", \"0.023\", \"1.7x\", \"Weak — near noise\"]\n          - [\"OpenVLA\", \"Object\", \"0.121\", \"0.076\", \"1.6x\", \"Moderate but untrained also high\"]\n          - [\"OpenVLA\", \"Long (OFT)\", \"0.004\", \"0.016\", \"0.25x\", \"FAIL — no collapse\"]\n          - [\"TracVLA\", \"Goal\", \"0.090\", \"0.048\", \"1.9x\", \"Weak\"]\n          - [\"TracVLA\", \"Spatial\", \"0.138\", \"0.016\", \"8.6x\", \"Strong\"]\n          - [\"TracVLA\", \"Object\", \"0.294\", \"0.009\", \"32.7x\", \"Strong\"]\n          - [\"TracVLA\", \"Long\", \"0.198\", \"0.028\", \"7.1x\", \"Strong\"]\n          - [\"NORA\", \"Goal\", \"0.691\", \"0.044\", \"15.7x\", \"Extreme — outlier?\"]\n          - [\"NORA\", \"Spatial\", \"0.302\", \"0.037\", \"8.2x\", \"Strong\"]\n      - title: \"Matrix Coverage and Gaps\"\n        columns: [\"Metric\", \"Value\", \"Worst Interpretation\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Cells filled\", \"10/12\", \"NORA Object/Long missing — incomplete\"]\n          - [\"Clear collapse (>0.10)\", \"6/10\", \"Only 60% cells show clear effect\"]\n          - [\"Weak/absent\", \"4/10\", \"40% cells ambiguous or failed\"]\n          - [\"Delta range\", \"0.004–0.691\", \"172x range — not 'consistent'\"]\n          - [\"Peak layer std\", \"6.2\", \"High variability in where collapse occurs\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Heatmap: 3×4 matrix 用 color intensity 表示 delta magnitude，4 cells 用虚线边框标注 'weak/absent'，2 cells 灰色标注 'missing'\"\n      - \"Box plot: delta distribution across 10 cells，标注 median=0.096 和 IQR 显示 high spread\"\n    analysis: >\n      Worst tier 核心判定：cross-architecture R² exit collapse 是方向一致的（9/10 trained>untrained）\n      但 magnitude 高度不一致（0.004-0.691）。\"Architecture-independent signature\" claim\n      在 worst tier 下被降级为 \"a directionally consistent but magnitude-variable observation\"。\n      Reviewer 要求：(1) 解释 magnitude variation 的 mechanism（为什么 NORA 15x 于 OpenVLA？），\n      (2) 排除 training procedure confound（自训练 vs 社区 checkpoint），\n      (3) 提供 NLP fine-tuning baseline 排除 decoder-only generic effect。\n      Framework reframe：exit collapse 降为 \"one of the patterns detected by our framework\"\n      而非 \"the architecture-independent signature\"。强调 framework 能 systematically\n      reveal cross-architecture variation 而非 uniformity。\n\n  - name: \"Cross-Architecture L1 Attention (D090 Training-Induced vs Base-Model)\"\n    plan_id: \"cross_arch_l1_attention\"\n    description: \"3 架构的 L1 instruction-dominant heads 对比——D090 区分 training vs base-model effects\"\n    expected_results:\n      openvla_trained_l1_heads: 24\n      openvla_untrained_l1_heads: 0\n      openvla_oxe_l1_heads: 25\n      tracvla_trained_l1_heads: [27, 30]\n      tracvla_untrained_l1_heads: 32\n      nora_trained_l1_heads: [12, 13]\n      nora_untrained_l1_heads: [13, 14]\n      training_induced: false\n      base_model_dependent: true\n    result_rationale: >\n      D090 发现 L1 head count 是 base-model-dependent 而非 training-induced。\n      Worst tier 解读：这是论文最严重的自我削弱。Reviewer：\"你们自己证明了\n      L1 routing——论文最 visually striking 的结果（0→9→24 heads gradient）——\n      不是训练学到的。TracVLA untrained 已经 32/32 全极化，NORA untrained 已经\n      13/16。那 VLA training 到底贡献了什么？剩下的 training-induced effects\n      只有 R² exit collapse 和 CF sensitivity。但 exit collapse 可能是 generic\n      fine-tuning effect（见上），CF sensitivity 可能只是 'model produces\n      different outputs for different inputs' 的 trivial restatement。\n      你们把自己的 contribution 证伪到只剩一个 questionable finding。\"\n\n      D090 被解读为 \"VLA training 的独特效果只剩 exit collapse 一个，contribution 太薄\"。\n      即使 exit collapse confirmed in 6/10 cells，作为唯一 training-induced effect\n      支撑一篇 CoRL paper 太单薄。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"L1 Heads: Base-Model Dominance (D090)\"\n        columns: [\"Architecture\", \"Backbone\", \"Trained\", \"Untrained\", \"Training Effect\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"OpenVLA\", \"Llama-2-7B\", \"24/32\", \"0/32 (random)\", \"Artifact: random init has no LM ability\"]\n          - [\"OpenVLA\", \"OXE-pretrained\", \"24/32\", \"25/32 (OXE)\", \"Zero: OXE already saturated\"]\n          - [\"TracVLA\", \"Phi-3-mini\", \"27-30/32\", \"32/32 (VLM)\", \"Negative: training reduces heads\"]\n          - [\"NORA\", \"Qwen2.5-VL-3B\", \"12-13/16\", \"13-14/16\", \"Zero: same before and after\"]\n      - title: \"Remaining Training-Induced Effects After D090\"\n        columns: [\"Effect\", \"Evidence Strength\", \"VLA-Specificity\", \"Contribution Weight\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"R² exit collapse\", \"6/10 cells\", \"Questionable (need NLP control)\", \"Thin\"]\n          - [\"CF sensitivity\", \"11/12 settings\", \"Moderate (empty ≠ original)\", \"Thin\"]\n          - [\"L1 head count\", \"REMOVED by D090\", \"Base-model artifact\", \"Zero\"]\n          - [\"Total remaining\", \"—\", \"—\", \"Near-minimal for CoRL\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Before/After D090 contribution diagram: 三个 pillars 砍掉一个，剩两个标注 'questionable'\"\n    analysis: >\n      D090 在 worst tier 下是论文最大的 self-inflicted wound。Framework reframe\n      的关键 pivot：把 D090 从 \"limitation that weakens the paper\" 转为\n      \"framework's key analytical capability\"——\"our framework can distinguish\n      training-induced from pre-existing properties, which is crucial for\n      understanding what VLA training actually does.\" 这种 reframe 让 D090\n      变成 framework 的 selling point 而非 paper 的 weakness。但 reviewer\n      可能看穿这个 rhetorical move。\n\n  - name: \"Cross-Architecture Counterfactual Sensitivity\"\n    plan_id: \"cross_arch_cf\"\n    description: \"3 架构的 counterfactual instruction sensitivity 对比\"\n    expected_results:\n      openvla_object_d: 1.21\n      tracvla_goal_d: 1.52\n      tracvla_spatial_d: 1.33\n      tracvla_object_d: 1.21\n      tracvla_long_d: 1.47\n      nora_goal_cos_saturated: 1.0\n      cf_sensitivity_ratio_range: [2, 8]\n      empty_always_top: \"11/12 settings\"\n      openvla_long_anomaly: \"shuffled > empty\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      CF sensitivity 是仅存的两个 training-induced effects 之一（D090 后）。\n      Worst tier 攻击：Reviewer：\"counterfactual sensitivity 只是说 'trained model\n      produces different outputs for different instructions'——这是 ANY trained\n      language model 的 basic capability，不是 VLA-specific routing。你们的\n      untrained model 是 random init（OpenVLA）或 base VLM without action head（TracVLA/NORA），\n      当然 CF sensitivity 低——它们根本不是 functional models。这不是 fair comparison。\n      一个 fair comparison 是 Llama-2 fine-tuned on NLP 的 counterfactual sensitivity——\n      如果它也显示类似 pattern，那 CF sensitivity 是 instruction following 的\n      generic property 而非 VLA routing。\"\n\n      NORA 的 cosine distance = 1.0（saturated）也有问题——这可能是 numerical artifact\n      而非 genuine effect（Qwen2.5-VL 的 exit layer 表征可能在不同 instruction 下\n      彻底 orthogonal 由于某种 architectural reason，而非 VLA training effect）。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"CF Sensitivity: Trained vs Untrained (Worst Interpretation)\"\n        columns: [\"Architecture\", \"Suite\", \"Trained d\", \"Untrained (cos)\", \"Ratio\", \"Reviewer Critique\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"OpenVLA\", \"Object\", \"1.21\", \"0.569\", \"2.1x\", \"Moderate, within generic fine-tuning range\"]\n          - [\"TracVLA\", \"Goal\", \"1.52\", \"0.153\", \"9.9x\", \"Strong but unfair: untrained=VLM base\"]\n          - [\"TracVLA\", \"Spatial\", \"1.33\", \"0.180\", \"7.4x\", \"Same unfair comparison\"]\n          - [\"TracVLA\", \"Object\", \"1.21\", \"0.185\", \"6.5x\", \"Same unfair comparison\"]\n          - [\"TracVLA\", \"Long\", \"1.47\", \"0.173\", \"8.5x\", \"Same unfair comparison\"]\n          - [\"NORA\", \"Goal\", \"saturated (1.0)\", \"0.081\", \"12.3x\", \"Numerical artifact? exit layer orthogonal\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Paired bar chart 标注 'unfair baseline' 在 untrained bars 上\"\n    analysis: >\n      CF sensitivity 在 worst tier 下保持 directionally valid 但\n      fair comparison 被质疑。关键缺失控制：NLP-finetuned LLM 的 CF sensitivity。\n      Framework reframe：CF analysis 降为 \"framework capability demonstration\"，\n      future work 建议跨 domain（NLP/vision/robotics）对比 CF sensitivity。\n\n  - name: \"Three-Tier Routing Gradient (D094)\"\n    plan_id: \"three_tier_gradient\"\n    description: \"VLM base → OXE-pretrained VLA → task-finetuned VLA 三层级路由梯度\"\n    expected_results:\n      tier1_l1_heads: [0, 32]\n      tier1_cf_sensitivity: \"<0.2\"\n      tier1_exit_collapse: false\n      tier2_l1_heads: 25\n      tier2_cf_d: 1.048\n      tier2_exit_collapse: false\n      tier3_exit_collapse: true\n      tier3_cf_d: [1.2, 1.5]\n      gradient_narrative: \"routing emerges at VLM→VLA, reshapes at general→specific\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      三层级梯度被驳为 post-hoc narrative。Worst tier 核心问题：Tier-2 只有一个\n      数据点（OpenVLA OXE-pretrained）。Reviewer：\"你们的 three-tier gradient\n      有 multiple Tier-1 数据点（TracVLA Phi-3-Vision, NORA Qwen2.5-VL）和\n      multiple Tier-3 数据点（3 arch × 4 suites），但 Tier-2 只有 ONE 数据点\n      （openvla-7b OXE pretrained）。Three-tier gradient 需要 at least 3\n      intermediate points 才能建立 gradient 而非 step function。你实际上只有\n      step function：VLM (no routing) → VLA (routing)。'Gradient' 这个词\n      暗示 continuous variation，但你只有 binary transition + 1 intermediate。\"\n\n      更致命的是 Tier-2 的 L1 heads（25/32）几乎与 Tier-3（24/32）相同——\n      D090 已经证明 L1 heads 是 base-model-dependent。所以 Tier-2→Tier-3\n      transition 的 routing 变化主要体现在 exit collapse（有/无）和\n      CF pattern（general/task-specific）——但这些效应量很小且可能是\n      generic fine-tuning effect。\n\n      三层级叙事的第三个问题：没有第四层（如 multi-task→single-task fine-tuning）\n      来验证 gradient 是 monotonic 的。如果 further specialization 反而\n      reduces routing（如 libero_finetuned 数据中 L31 exit engagement 18→0），\n      那 gradient narrative 不成立——routing 不是 monotonically increasing\n      with specialization。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Three-Tier Gradient: Data Sparsity (Worst-Tier)\"\n        columns: [\"Tier\", \"Description\", \"N data points\", \"Evidence\", \"Reviewer Critique\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Tier 1: VLM base\", \"No action training\", \"3 (Phi-3, Qwen2.5, random)\", \"No collapse, low CF\", \"Adequate N\"]\n          - [\"Tier 2: OXE-pretrained\", \"General action training\", \"1 (openvla-7b ONLY)\", \"No collapse, strong CF, strong L1\", \"N=1, cannot establish gradient\"]\n          - [\"Tier 3: Task-finetuned\", \"Task-specific training\", \"~10 (3 arch × 4 suites)\", \"Collapse + task CF\", \"Adequate N\"]\n          - [\"Verdict\", \"—\", \"—\", \"—\", \"Step function, not gradient\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Gradient diagram 中 Tier-2 标注 'N=1' 并用虚线连接，质疑 gradient claim\"\n    analysis: >\n      Worst tier 下三层级梯度必须移除或降为 \"preliminary observation\"。\n      Framework reframe：不 claim gradient，改为 \"framework enables comparison\n      across training stages\"——展示 framework 能分析不同训练阶段，\n      但不 claim 发现了 systematic gradient。Future work 建议收集更多\n      Tier-2 数据点（不同的 OXE-pretrained checkpoints、不同的 pretraining\n      datasets）来测试 gradient hypothesis。\n\n  - name: \"OpenVLA Goal Standardized Pipeline (RUNNING)\"\n    plan_id: \"openvla_goal_standardized_v1\"\n    description: \"OpenVLA LIBERO-Goal 标准化全流程——统一方法和指标的 re-run\"\n    expected_results:\n      r2_exit_collapse_delta: 0.07\n      l1_instruction_dominant: 24\n      cf_empty_d: 0.98\n      cf_sensitivity_ratio: 3.5\n      cross_instruction_accuracy: 1.0\n      rsa_peak_layer: 12\n    result_rationale: >\n      RUNNING 实验。Worst tier 预测：结果与已有 OpenVLA Goal 数据基本一致\n      （exit delta≈0.07, L1 heads≈24），因为使用相同 checkpoint。\n      但 standardized pipeline 可能暴露之前分散实验的 inconsistency——\n      例如不同实验使用了略微不同的 hyperparameters（probe architecture,\n      learning rate, seed）导致数字不完全 match。Reviewer 会注意到\n      \"为什么你需要 re-run standardized pipeline？之前的数字不可靠吗？\"\n      这暗示之前的 ad-hoc 实验流程不够 rigorous。\n      在 worst tier 下，standardized re-run 得到 slightly different numbers\n      (e.g., exit delta 0.07 vs 之前的 0.069) 会被解读为 \"results are\n      hyperparameter-sensitive\"。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Standardized vs Original: Consistency Check\"\n        columns: [\"Metric\", \"Original\", \"Standardized\", \"Delta\", \"Concern\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"R² exit delta\", \"0.069\", \"0.070\", \"+0.001\", \"Consistent but trivial\"]\n          - [\"L1 instr-dom heads\", \"24/32\", \"24/32\", \"0\", \"Identical\"]\n          - [\"CF empty d\", \"0.968\", \"0.980\", \"+0.012\", \"Consistent\"]\n          - [\"RSA peak\", \"L12\", \"L12\", \"0\", \"Identical\"]\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      Standardized pipeline 在 worst tier 下的隐含风险：承认之前的实验\n      不够 standardized，可能让 reviewer 质疑所有之前的数字。\n      但如果数字高度一致，也可以作为 robustness evidence。\n      Framework reframe：强调 standardized pipeline 是 framework 的\n      核心贡献之一——\"plug-and-play analysis toolkit\"。\n\n  - name: \"OpenVLA Spatial Standardized Pipeline (RUNNING)\"\n    plan_id: \"openvla_spatial_standardized_v1\"\n    description: \"OpenVLA LIBERO-Spatial 标准化全流程\"\n    expected_results:\n      r2_exit_collapse_delta: 0.04\n      l1_instruction_dominant: 24\n      cf_empty_d: 0.94\n      cf_sensitivity_ratio: 3.0\n      exit_collapse_weak: true\n      matrix_cell_verdict: \"weak — borderline\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      RUNNING 实验，worst tier 核心关注。预测 exit delta 仅 0.04——\n      显著弱于 OpenVLA Object (0.121) 和其他架构。原因：\n      (1) LIBERO-Spatial 的 action 空间以位置 reasoning 为主，\n      exit layer 需要保留更多 spatial information 来输出精确 actions，\n      所以 collapse 较弱。(2) OpenVLA 在 Spatial task 上的 fine-tuning\n      quality 可能较低（Spatial 是最难的 LIBERO suite），\n      训练不充分导致 exit reorganization 不完全。(3) 如果 untrained\n      也有 delta≈0.023，则 training effect ratio 仅 1.7x——\n      在统计上可能 borderline significant。\n\n      这个结果直接影响 matrix 的 story：OpenVLA 的 4 个 suite 中\n      2 个（Spatial 0.04, Long 0.004）weak/absent，只有 Object (0.121)\n      和 Goal (0.07) moderate。社区标准 checkpoint 的 2/4 suites\n      不支持 exit collapse = 严重的 generalizability concern。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"OpenVLA Cross-Suite Exit Collapse (Worst-Tier)\"\n        columns: [\"Suite\", \"Trained Delta\", \"Verdict\", \"Paper Implication\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Goal\", \"0.070\", \"Moderate\", \"Supports claim with caveats\"]\n          - [\"Spatial\", \"0.040\", \"Weak\", \"Borderline — weakens universality\"]\n          - [\"Object\", \"0.121\", \"Moderate-Strong\", \"Best OpenVLA cell\"]\n          - [\"Long (OFT)\", \"0.004\", \"Absent\", \"Outlier — OFT confound\"]\n          - [\"Overall\", \"mean=0.059\", \"Weak-Moderate\", \"OpenVLA is the WEAKEST architecture\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"OpenVLA 4-suite exit collapse bar chart 标注 'community checkpoint' 并与 TracVLA/NORA 对比——OpenVLA consistently lowest\"\n    analysis: >\n      OpenVLA Spatial 弱结果是 worst tier 最关键的预测。如果确认，\n      论文面临 \"社区 checkpoint 最弱\" 的尴尬叙事——reviewer 会问\n      \"如果你们用社区标准 checkpoint 复现你们的发现，效果最弱，\n      这是否说明 strong exit collapse 是你们自训练流程的 artifact？\"\n      Framework reframe 可以 acknowledge OpenVLA 作为 \"weaker case\"\n      并 argue \"our framework's value is precisely in revealing such\n      cross-architecture variation\"。\n\n  - name: \"D090 Training-Induced vs Base-Model Distinction Synthesis\"\n    plan_id: \"d090_synthesis\"\n    description: \"综合分析：VLA training 实际贡献了什么——D090 后的 contribution auditing\"\n    expected_results:\n      training_induced_effects: [\"R² exit collapse (6/10 cells)\", \"CF sensitivity (11/12 settings)\"]\n      base_model_effects: [\"L1 head count\", \"deep-layer probe stability\"]\n      removed_from_contribution: [\"L1 routing gradient (0→9→24)\", \"attention reorganization\"]\n      remaining_unique_contribution: \"thin — 1-2 effects, both questionable VLA-specificity\"\n      reviewer_expected_reaction: \"contribution too thin for CoRL\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      D090 移除了最 visually striking 的结果（L1 head gradient）后，\n      论文的 unique contribution audit 在 worst tier 下：\n      (1) R² exit collapse — 6/10 cells 确认但 magnitude 高度可变，\n      可能是 generic fine-tuning effect（缺 NLP control）。\n      (2) CF sensitivity — 11/12 settings trained > untrained，\n      但 unfair baseline（untrained = random init 或 VLM without action head）。\n      (3) 三层级梯度 — N=1 at Tier-2，post-hoc narrative。\n\n      至少 2 个 reviewer 给 reject，原因集中在：\n      - \"What does VLA training ACTUALLY do that's unique? After your own D090\n        analysis, the answer is 'exit collapse' — which may not be VLA-specific.\"\n      - \"Practical value unclear: knowing about exit collapse doesn't help\n        build better VLAs. No behavioral validation, no design implications tested.\"\n      - \"The paper's main strength is the experimental framework, not the findings.\n        But CoRL reviews papers for findings, not frameworks.\"\n\n      Expected reviewer avg score: 3.5 (range 3.0-4.5)\n      Accept probability: 0.10 (range 0.05-0.20)\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Contribution Audit After D090 (Worst-Tier)\"\n        columns: [\"Claimed Contribution\", \"Status Post-D090\", \"VLA-Specific?\", \"Reviewer Verdict\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"L1 routing (0→9→24)\", \"REMOVED — base-model artifact\", \"No\", \"Cannot claim\"]\n          - [\"R² exit collapse\", \"Retained but 4/10 cells weak\", \"Questionable\", \"Need NLP control\"]\n          - [\"CF sensitivity\", \"Retained, 11/12 settings\", \"Questionable\", \"Unfair baseline\"]\n          - [\"Three-tier gradient\", \"N=1 at Tier-2\", \"Thin\", \"Post-hoc narrative\"]\n          - [\"Experimental framework\", \"Intact\", \"Yes\", \"Main contribution in reframe\"]\n          - [\"Metric dissociation (RSA/CKA/R²)\", \"Intact\", \"Yes\", \"Methodological\"]\n      - title: \"Worst-Tier Reviewer Score Prediction\"\n        columns: [\"Reviewer\", \"Score\", \"Main Concern\", \"Accept/Reject\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"R1 (generalizability)\", \"3\", \"40% matrix cells weak; no NLP control; contribution too thin\", \"Reject\"]\n          - [\"R2 (methodology)\", \"5\", \"Framework is solid and reusable; findings secondary but valid\", \"Weak Accept\"]\n          - [\"R3 (practical value)\", \"3\", \"No behavioral validation; no design implications tested; CoRL wants practical\", \"Reject\"]\n          - [\"Mean\", \"3.67\", \"2 reject, 1 weak accept\", \"Likely Reject\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Contribution pyramid: framework at base (strong), exit collapse in middle (questionable), L1 routing crossed out at top\"\n    analysis: >\n      Worst tier 核心结论：D090 的 honest analysis 是 scientifically correct\n      但 strategically devastating。论文自己证明了 3 个原 claim pillars 中\n      1 个是 base-model artifact（L1 routing），另外 2 个（exit collapse, CF）\n      缺少 critical controls。剩余的 unique contribution 太薄支撑 CoRL paper。\n\n      Reframe 路径（accept probability 0.10→0.20 的条件）：\n      (1) C1 升级为主贡献——framework 本身（factorial design + 4 methods + 3 arch validation）\n      是可复用工具，CoRL 有 benchmark/framework paper 先例。\n      (2) R² collapse 和 CF sensitivity 降为 \"findings the framework reveals\"——\n      不 claim VLA-specific，改为 \"training-induced effects observable through our framework\"。\n      (3) D090 repackage 为 \"framework's distinguishing capability\"——\n      能区分 training-induced vs pre-existing 是 framework 的 unique selling point。\n      (4) 增加 2-3 个 additional analyses（per-layer information flow entropy,\n      cross-task representation transfer analysis）增强 framework demonstration value。\n      (5) 三层级梯度移除或降为 1 段 future work。\n      (6) 明确 roadmap：\"framework enables future closed-loop behavioral studies\"。\n      (7) Title 从 \"Architecture-Independent Routing in VLAs\" 改为\n      \"A Systematic Framework for Analyzing Instruction Processing in VLAs\"。\n\n      即使全部执行，worst tier accept probability 仍只 0.05-0.20——\n      因为 CoRL 倾向 \"systems + results\" 而非 \"analysis + framework\"。\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":16939,"cache_read_input_tokens":62853,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":16939},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"506abc2d-d23e-45e9-955e-d6d2abc337cb","uuid":"2924dd8f-4c0b-42c6-87d4-e7bce152a860"}
{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"api_error_status":null,"duration_ms":470598,"duration_api_ms":471385,"num_turns":4,"result":"Now I have full context. Let me generate the worst-tier predictions for the D095 cross-architecture upgrade scenario.\n\n```yaml\ntier: worst\nnarrative_guidance: >\n  跨架构证据被质疑为不充分或 trivial。Reviewer 论证 R² exit collapse 是 decoder-only 架构的通用表征压缩\n  而非 VLA-specific effect（\"any supervised fine-tuning on decoder-only LLM would produce similar exit-layer\n  information loss\"）。OpenVLA Spatial 无明显 exit collapse（RUNNING 实验结果弱），矩阵空洞（NORA Object/Long\n  缺失）使 \"architecture-independent\" claim 站不住。D090 的 base-model-dependent 发现被解读为 \"contribution\n  只剩 exit collapse 一个 training-induced effect，太薄\"。三层级梯度仅 1 个 Tier-2 数据点（OpenVLA OXE），\n  被驳为 post-hoc narrative。Behavioral validation 完全缺失在 CoRL（robotics venue）被视为 near-fatal。\n  Reframe 方向：从 \"architecture-independent routing signature\" 转为 \"systematic diagnostic framework\n  for VLA internal representations\"。C1 (framework) 升为主要贡献，R² collapse 和 CF sensitivity\n  降为 \"findings the framework reveals\"。增加 per-layer information flow entropy、cross-task transfer\n  analysis 等 framework demonstration analyses 增强贡献厚度。\n\nimagined_experiments:\n  - name: \"SigLIP+Projector RSA vs Full VLA vs DINO\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_001\"\n    description: \"SigLIP+Projector RSA 对比 Full VLA 和 DINO，证明 action-relevant 结构源自 frozen vision encoder\"\n    expected_results:\n      siglip_projector_rsa: 0.615\n      trained_with_inst_rsa: 0.488\n      untrained_with_inst_rsa: 0.485\n      dino_rsa: 0.388\n      llm_degradation_delta: 0.127\n    result_rationale: >\n      数据已完成不变。但在 worst D095 下，此实验仅覆盖 OpenVLA 一种架构。Reviewer 攻击：\n      \"SigLIP+DinoSigLIP projector 的 RSA=0.615 是 OpenVLA-specific 的 frozen encoder 观察。\n      TracVLA 用 Phi-3-Vision 的不同 encoder，NORA 用 InternViT——你们没测这些 encoder 的 RSA。\n      单架构 encoder analysis 不能 claim architecture-independent。\" 在 framework reframe 下，\n      此实验降为 \"framework 在 OpenVLA 上的 case study\"，不再是 core contribution。\n      LLM degradation（0.615→0.488）本身仍有价值但被限定为 \"observed in Llama-2-7B backbone\"。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"SigLIP RSA Scope Limitation (Worst-Tier)\"\n        columns: [\"Source\", \"RSA\", \"Architecture Coverage\", \"Worst Interpretation\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"SigLIP+Proj\", \"0.615\", \"OpenVLA only\", \"Cannot generalize to other VLA encoders\"]\n          - [\"VLA trained\", \"0.488\", \"OpenVLA only\", \"Llama-2 specific LLM degradation\"]\n          - [\"VLA untrained\", \"0.485\", \"OpenVLA only\", \"Random-init Llama-2 specific\"]\n          - [\"DINO\", \"0.388\", \"Standalone\", \"Reference baseline, unaffected\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Bar chart 标注 'OpenVLA only' 在每个 bar 上方，突显 single-arch limitation\"\n    analysis: >\n      Framework reframe 下此实验从 C1 core evidence 降为 Section 4.1 case study。\n      价值在于 demonstrate framework 的 encoder-LLM decomposition 能力，而非 claim 本身。\n      Reviewer 不会因此给分但也不会因此扣分——neutral contribution in worst tier。\n\n  - name: \"DINO baseline RSA\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_002\"\n    description: \"Standalone vision model 参照基线\"\n    expected_results:\n      dino_rsa: 0.388\n      dino_action_R2: 0.687\n      dino_subtask_auc: 0.972\n    result_rationale: >\n      数据不变。Worst 档下 DINO 的角色不变——纯视觉 baseline。但 reviewer 可能用 DINO\n      的高 action R²=0.687 攻击论文：\"DINO（self-supervised, 无 language, 无 action training）\n      的 action probe R² 已 0.687，你们声称的 VLA training-induced R² exit collapse\n      只是从 0.68 掉到 0.60——这可能只是 fine-tuning 过程中正常的 representation compression，\n      任何 supervised fine-tuning 都会导致 exit layer 表征质量下降。\"\n    tables: []\n    figures_description:\n      - \"DINO 作为 'no-training baseline' 的 R²=0.687 标注在所有 cross-arch R² exit collapse 图上，质疑 collapse 的意义\"\n    analysis: >\n      DINO baseline 在 worst tier 被 reviewer 用来论证 exit collapse 的 trivial nature：\n      如果未训练模型 R²=0.687 而训练后 exit R² 下降到 0.55-0.60，这可能只是 supervised\n      learning 的通用 representation bottleneck 而非 VLA-specific routing。\n\n  - name: \"Per-layer RSA degradation curve\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_003\"\n    description: \"追踪 RSA 从 projector output 到 LLM 各层的变换轨迹\"\n    expected_results:\n      proj_rsa: 0.615\n      trained_peak_rsa: 0.488\n      trained_peak_layer: 9\n      untrained_peak_rsa: 0.485\n      untrained_peak_layer: 12\n      proj_to_l1_drop: 0.13\n      inverted_u_pattern: true\n    result_rationale: >\n      数据不变。Worst D095 下，inverted-U pattern 只在 OpenVLA (Llama-2) 上验证。\n      TracVLA 和 NORA 的 RSA per-layer curve 未做（只做了 R² probe），所以 \"inverted-U\n      is architecture-independent\" 无法 claim。Reviewer：\"RSA inverted-U 可能是 Llama-2\n      的 32 层架构特有的——Phi-3-mini 同为 32 层但 tokenization 不同，Qwen2.5-VL 是 36 层\n      且 GQA 架构，per-layer dynamics 可能完全不同。\" 此外 CKA 反转（plan_009）使\n      RSA 本身作为 metric 的 authority 被削弱。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"RSA Inverted-U Architecture Coverage\"\n        columns: [\"Architecture\", \"RSA Per-Layer Done?\", \"Pattern\", \"Worst Interpretation\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"OpenVLA (Llama-2-7B)\", \"Yes\", \"Inverted-U\", \"Only confirmed case\"]\n          - [\"TracVLA (Phi-3-mini)\", \"No\", \"Unknown\", \"Cannot claim generalization\"]\n          - [\"NORA (Qwen2.5-VL-3B)\", \"No\", \"Unknown\", \"Cannot claim generalization\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Per-layer RSA curve 只有 OpenVLA 一条线，旁边标 '?' 表示其他架构未验证\"\n    analysis: >\n      Framework reframe 下，inverted-U 成为 \"framework 在 OpenVLA 上发现的 pattern\" 而非\n      \"architecture-independent finding\"。可以保留为 case study 但不能 claim generality。\n      补救路径：增加 TracVLA/NORA 的 per-layer RSA 分析作为 framework demonstration。\n\n  - name: \"Output head analysis\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_004\"\n    description: \"SigLIP+projector frozen 确认, LLM 权重变化不传导到表征\"\n    expected_results:\n      vision_projector_cos_sim: 1.0\n      llm_rel_change_range: [1.22, 1.37]\n      head_vs_llm_ratio: 1.12\n      shallow_adaptation_gate: \"FAIL\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      数据不变。Worst D095 下，此实验对 framework 贡献有价值——它证明 framework 能\n      区分 frozen 和 trainable 组件。但 reviewer 可能指出：\"这是 trivial verification——\n      OpenVLA 的训练代码明确 freeze 了 vision encoder，你们只是验证了代码做了它说的事。\n      这不是 experimental finding，是 implementation confirmation。\" 在 framework paper 中，\n      这降为 Section 3 的 methodology validation paragraph，不占独立篇幅。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      Worst tier 下此实验贡献接近零——reviewer 视为 trivial。但在 framework reframe 下\n      可以包装为 \"framework 的 component attribution 能力 demonstration\"：展示 framework\n      如何分离 encoder/projector/LLM 各组件的贡献。贡献在方法论而非 finding。\n\n  - name: \"6 probing methods × 2 benchmarks 系统验证\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_005\"\n    description: \"系统性验证 trained ≈ untrained 表征结构\"\n    expected_results:\n      trained_vs_untrained_delta: 0.003\n      all_methods_consistent: true\n      cross_benchmark_replicated: true\n    result_rationale: >\n      Orphaned 但子实验完成。Worst D095 下，trained ≈ untrained 的 RSA 结论仍成立\n      但意义被 D090 reinterpret：Reviewer 说 \"trained ≈ untrained 在 distributed\n      representation (RSA/R²) 上不奇怪——frozen encoder 输出相同 L0 features，LLM\n      的 fine-tuning 主要影响 exit layer action head，中间层表征 naturally preserved。\n      这是 transfer learning 的常识，不需要 6 种方法来验证。\" 在 framework paper 中，\n      6 methods consistency 仍是 methodology 亮点——展示 framework 的 multi-method\n      triangulation 能力。但 finding 本身被视为 expected。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"6 Methods Consistency (Worst-Tier Reinterpretation)\"\n        columns: [\"Method\", \"Trained-Untrained Delta\", \"Reviewer Interpretation\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"RSA\", \"0.003\", \"Expected: frozen encoder dominates\"]\n          - [\"R² probe\", \"0.015\", \"Expected: similar L0 inputs\"]\n          - [\"CKA\", \"-0.006\", \"Reversal: undermines RSA conclusion\"]\n          - [\"Action probe\", \"0.045\", \"Marginal: routing exists but small\"]\n          - [\"Delta probe\", \"0.011\", \"Expected: similar input structure\"]\n          - [\"Classification\", \"0.001\", \"Trivially easy for both\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"6-method radar chart 显示 consistency，但加标注 'Expected under frozen encoder'\"\n    analysis: >\n      Worst tier 下 6 methods consistency 从 \"strong evidence for Claim 3\" 降为\n      \"thorough but unsurprising verification\"。Framework reframe 下，价值在于\n      demonstrate framework 的 multi-method coverage 而非 finding novelty。\n\n  - name: \"Instruction ablation\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_006\"\n    description: \"去掉 instruction text 测 RSA 变化\"\n    expected_results:\n      delta_with_vs_no_inst: 0.004\n      gate_judgment: \"FAIL — instruction 无影响 on RSA\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      数据不变。Worst D095 下，instruction 对 RSA 无影响是 OpenVLA-specific 观察。\n      Reviewer：\"RSA 测量 image token 的几何结构，当然不受 instruction 影响——image tokens\n      在 causal mask 下看不到 instruction tokens，这在你们 C1 里已经承认是 structural\n      guarantee。所以 Δ=0.004 不是 finding，是 sanity check。\" 更严重的是，TracVLA\n      和 NORA 上未做此 ablation，所以即使从 framework demonstration 角度也只是单架构。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      Worst tier 下从 \"Claim 3 evidence\" 降为 \"expected sanity check\"。\n      但在 framework paper 中，instruction ablation 仍可作为 framework 的\n      \"controlled manipulation\" capability demonstration，只是不能 claim novelty。\n\n  - name: \"2×2 matrix (training × instruction)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_007\"\n    description: \"四条件全收敛验证\"\n    expected_results:\n      four_cell_range: [0.48, 0.49]\n      bootstrap_ci_includes_0: true\n      training_effect: 0.003\n      instruction_effect: 0.004\n    result_rationale: >\n      数据不变。Worst D095 下 2×2 矩阵仍是 clean experimental design 但\n      被视为 \"confirms the obvious\"。Reviewer：\"frozen encoder + causal mask\n      已经预测了这个 null result。你的 2×2 design 很好但发现的是 expected outcome——\n      这不是 contribution，是 verification。\" 在 framework paper 中，2×2 factorial\n      design 可以作为 framework reusability 的 exemplar（\"researchers can apply\n      this factorial approach to any VLA\"），但 the finding itself 不计分。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"2×2 Matrix (Worst-Tier: Expected Null)\"\n        columns: [\"Condition\", \"RSA\", \"Reviewer Verdict\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Trained + Inst\", \"0.488\", \"Expected: frozen encoder dominates\"]\n          - [\"Trained - Inst\", \"0.489\", \"Expected: image RSA independent of text\"]\n          - [\"Untrained + Inst\", \"0.485\", \"Expected: same encoder, same RSA\"]\n          - [\"Untrained - Inst\", \"0.480\", \"Expected: null result confirmed\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"2×2 heatmap 标注 'Expected null result under frozen encoder hypothesis'\"\n    analysis: >\n      Framework paper reframe 下，2×2 matrix 的价值从 \"empirical finding\" 转为\n      \"exemplar of framework's factorial design capability\"。论文可以说\n      \"our framework enables systematic 2×2 factorial decomposition of training\n      and instruction effects\"——贡献在方法论可复用性而非结果。\n\n  - name: \"Random instruction control\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_008\"\n    description: \"随机/无意义 instruction 替代验证 RSA 不受 instruction content 影响\"\n    expected_results:\n      normal_rsa: 0.489\n      random_rsa: 0.484\n      shuffled_rsa: 0.483\n      empty_rsa: 0.472\n      max_absolute_delta: 0.017\n      instruction_invariant: true\n    result_rationale: >\n      数据不变。与 plan_006/007 相同逻辑——causal mask 使 image token RSA\n      对 instruction 天然不变。四种 instruction 条件下 Δ<0.02 是 expected 而非 surprising。\n      Worst D095 的关键攻击面不在此实验本身，而在于论文用了三个 plan（006/007/008）\n      来验证一个 structurally guaranteed result，reviewer 会认为 \"过度验证 trivial\n      prediction，浪费篇幅\"。在 8 页限制下这 3 个实验应压缩为 1 段。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      Framework reframe 下，random instruction control 与 006/007 合并为\n      \"three-way invariance verification\" 单段，作为 framework sanity check\n      的示范。占 0.5 段而非独立 subsection。\n\n  - name: \"CKA verification\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_009\"\n    description: \"CKA 指标验证 RSA 发现的 metric robustness\"\n    expected_results:\n      cka_ordering: \"untrained > trained > projector > DINO (反转 RSA)\"\n      rsa_cka_dissociation: true\n      linear_cka_last_preaction: 0.127\n    result_rationale: >\n      数据不变。Worst D095 下 CKA-RSA dissociation 变得更致命。Reviewer：\n      \"你们声称 R² exit collapse 是 architecture-independent training effect，\n      但 CKA（另一种 representational similarity metric）显示 untrained > trained——\n      即训练反而增强了 global structure。如果换个 metric 就得到相反结论，\n      那 R² exit collapse 可能只是 metric artifact 而非 genuine information loss。\n      你们怎么证明 R² 比 CKA 更能捕捉 'action-relevant information'？\"\n      在 framework paper 中，metric dissociation 可以包装为 \"framework reveals\n      metric-dependent conclusions\"——但这削弱了所有 quantitative findings 的\n      authority，因为 reviewer 会质疑每个 metric 的选择。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Metric Ordering Reversal (Worst: Authority Crisis)\"\n        columns: [\"Metric\", \"Ordering\", \"Implication\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"RSA (geometric)\", \"SigLIP > T > U > DINO\", \"Training degrades geometry\"]\n          - [\"CKA (global)\", \"U > T > SigLIP > DINO\", \"Training preserves/improves structure\"]\n          - [\"R² (functional)\", \"T_readout > DINO ≈ Proj > T_img\", \"Training enables routing\"]\n          - [\"Reviewer question\", \"—\", \"Which metric is 'correct' for VLA evaluation?\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Triple ordering diagram 标注 '?' 在每条 ordering line 上——哪个 metric 才对？\"\n    analysis: >\n      Worst tier 下 CKA dissociation 是双刃剑。Framework reframe 可以用它\n      作为 \"why we need multi-metric frameworks\"（方法论贡献），但这同时\n      undermine 了 R² exit collapse 作为 \"the architecture-independent signature\"\n      的 clean narrative。如果 exit collapse 只在 R² 下明显而 CKA 下不成立，\n      reviewer 会要求 \"architecture-independent claim 必须 metric-independent\"。\n\n  - name: \"LIBERO-Spatial cross-benchmark 扩展\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_010\"\n    description: \"第三个 benchmark（LIBERO-Spatial）交叉验证\"\n    expected_results:\n      trained_image_mean_peak_R2: 0.696\n      trained_last_preaction_peak_R2: 0.675\n      untrained_image_mean_peak_R2: 0.673\n      untrained_last_preaction_peak_R2: 0.635\n      trained_exit_R2_delta: 0.04\n      bootstrap_significance_p: 0.001\n      cross_benchmark_consistency: \"partial\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      LIBERO-Spatial 数据已部分完成（plan_010 status=preparing 但 registry 有结果）。\n      Worst D095 下，此实验是 OpenVLA 的 within-architecture cross-benchmark，\n      不是 cross-architecture validation。Reviewer：\"你从 LIBERO-Goal 换到 LIBERO-Spatial\n      只是换了 task suite 而非换了 VLA 架构——这不解决 RC4 的核心问题。\"\n      更关键的是，Spatial 的 exit R² delta 只有 0.04（vs Goal 的 0.069），\n      说明 exit collapse strength 是 task-dependent 的。Worst 解读：\n      exit collapse 不是 fundamental property 而是 task difficulty proxy——\n      harder tasks (Spatial) 产生较弱 collapse 因为模型需要保留更多 exit-layer\n      information 来处理复杂空间推理。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Cross-Benchmark Exit Collapse Comparison\"\n        columns: [\"Benchmark\", \"Trained Exit Delta\", \"Untrained Exit Delta\", \"Training Effect\", \"Interpretation\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"LIBERO-Goal\", \"0.069\", \"0.015\", \"4.6x\", \"Moderate collapse\"]\n          - [\"LIBERO-Spatial\", \"0.040\", \"0.023\", \"1.7x\", \"Weak collapse, task-dependent\"]\n          - [\"LIBERO-Object\", \"0.121\", \"0.076\", \"1.6x\", \"Moderate but untrained also collapses\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Paired bar chart: Goal vs Spatial exit delta，显示 collapse 强度的 task dependency\"\n    analysis: >\n      Cross-benchmark 结果在 worst tier 下被解读为 exit collapse 是\n      task-complexity-dependent 而非 architectural invariant。如果 collapse\n      强度随任务变化，它更像是 training-specific adaptation 而非\n      fundamental routing reorganization。Framework reframe 可以 claim\n      \"our framework reveals task-dependent routing intensity\"——\n      但这削弱了 \"architecture-independent signature\" 的 universality。\n\n  - name: \"Full-layer R² scan\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_011\"\n    description: \"33 layers × 2 conditions × 2 aggregations = 132 probes 的 R² 全层扫描\"\n    expected_results:\n      trained_image_mean_peak: {layer: 8, R2: 0.655}\n      trained_last_preaction_peak: {layer: 13, R2: 0.678}\n      untrained_image_mean_peak: {layer: 0, R2: 0.640}\n      untrained_last_preaction_peak: {layer: 32, R2: 0.609}\n      trained_exit_R2: 0.422\n      untrained_exit_R2: 0.545\n      exit_collapse_delta: 0.123\n      best_vs_best_lastpre_delta: 0.069\n      best_vs_best_lastpre_p: 0.0001\n    result_rationale: >\n      数据不变（OpenVLA 单架构）。这是 R² exit collapse 的源头证据。\n      Worst D095 下的核心攻击：Reviewer A 论证 \"exit collapse 是 decoder-only\n      LLM 在 supervised fine-tuning 下的通用行为——last preaction token 在\n      exit layer 被 action head 'consume'，functional information 被转化为\n      action prediction 而非保留在 hidden state 中。这不是 VLA-specific routing，\n      而是任何 decoder-only model 做 seq2seq mapping 时的 normal information\n      bottleneck。你需要对比 LLM 在 NLP task fine-tuning 下的 exit layer R²\n      来排除这个 confound——但你没做这个 control。\"\n      Reviewer B 补充：\"untrained model（random init）的 last_preaction R²\n      在 L10-L13 pathological (≈0) 不是 exit collapse 的对照——random init\n      model 在深层的 R²≈0 只是说明随机权重不能解码信息，这与 trained model\n      的 exit collapse 机制完全不同。你实际上没有一个 clean baseline。\"\n    tables:\n      - title: \"R² Exit Collapse: Missing Control (Worst-Tier)\"\n        columns: [\"Condition\", \"Peak R²\", \"Exit R²\", \"Delta\", \"Reviewer Critique\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Trained\", \"0.678 (L13)\", \"0.422 (L32)\", \"0.256\", \"Could be generic fine-tuning bottleneck\"]\n          - [\"Untrained (random)\", \"0.609 (L32)\", \"n/a\", \"n/a\", \"Not a valid control for collapse\"]\n          - [\"Llama-2 base\", \"0.645 (L9)\", \"0.555 (L32)\", \"0.090\", \"Base LLM also shows mild decline\"]\n          - [\"NLP fine-tuned LLM\", \"???\", \"???\", \"???\", \"Missing: the critical control\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Per-layer R² curve 添加 'NLP fine-tuning control needed' 标注在 gap 区域\"\n    analysis: >\n      Worst tier 下 exit collapse 的 VLA-specificity 被根本性质疑。\n      缺少 NLP fine-tuned LLM 的 per-layer R² control 是最大 gap——\n      如果 Llama-2 fine-tuned on any supervised task 也显示类似 exit collapse，\n      那 VLA training 的 \"unique\" contribution 归零。Framework reframe 下，\n      collapse 降为 \"one of the patterns our framework detects\"，\n      VLA-specificity claim 移除，改为 \"future work: compare across fine-tuning domains\"。\n\n  - name: \"CLIP-ViT pretraining control\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_012\"\n    description: \"CLIP ViT-L 替代 SigLIP 区分 VL pretraining vs encoder quality\"\n    expected_results:\n      clip_rsa: 0.557\n      clip_R2: 0.587\n      clip_lt_dino_in_both: true\n      vl_pretraining_not_sufficient: true\n    result_rationale: >\n      数据已完成：CLIP RSA=0.557 < DINO cls=0.692，R²=0.587 < DINO R²=0.634。\n      VL pretraining 不优于 self-supervised。Worst D095 下，此结果被 reviewer\n      进一步延伸：\"你们的 CLIP < DINO 结果说明 vision encoder 质量不取决于\n      language supervision，那你们为什么还在论文里花大量篇幅讨论 instruction\n      routing？如果最好的 action representation 来自无 language 的 DINO，\n      那 VLA 的 instruction routing 可能是 overhead 而非 feature。\"\n      这挑战了整篇论文的前提——studying instruction routing in VLA 的意义。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Encoder Comparison: DINO Dominance Problem\"\n        columns: [\"Encoder\", \"RSA\", \"R²\", \"Has Language?\", \"Worst Implication\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"DINO cls\", \"0.692\", \"0.634\", \"No\", \"Best in both metrics without language\"]\n          - [\"SigLIP+Proj\", \"0.615\", \"0.630\", \"Yes\", \"VL pretraining inferior to DINO\"]\n          - [\"CLIP ViT-L\", \"0.557\", \"0.587\", \"Yes\", \"VL pretraining worst of three\"]\n          - [\"Implication\", \"—\", \"—\", \"—\", \"Language supervision hurts encoder quality?\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Scatter plot: RSA vs R² 显示 DINO 独占右上角，两个 VL encoders 均在左下\"\n    analysis: >\n      CLIP 结果在 worst tier 下不仅否定 VL pretraining 的 encoder quality claim，\n      更挑战论文研究 instruction routing 的 motivation：如果最好的 action\n      representations 来自无 language 的 encoder，instruction routing research\n      的 practical relevance 是什么？Framework reframe 可以 acknowledge 这个\n      tension 并 argue \"understanding routing is important precisely because\n      the relationship between language and action is non-obvious\"。\n\n  - name: \"Branch-split RSA\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_013\"\n    description: \"DinoSigLIP fused backbone 中 DINOv2 vs SigLIP branch 分离\"\n    expected_results:\n      dinov2_branch_rsa: 0.619\n      siglip_branch_rsa: 0.621\n      fused_rsa: 0.634\n      post_projector_rsa: 0.615\n    result_rationale: >\n      数据不变。DINOv2 ≈ SigLIP（Δ<0.002）在 fused backbone 内。\n      Worst D095 下，此实验仅适用于 OpenVLA 的 DinoSigLIP backbone。\n      TracVLA 用 Phi-3-Vision 的不同 vision encoder（SigLIP-based 但\n      架构不同），NORA 用 InternViT。Branch-split analysis 不可迁移到\n      其他架构。Reviewer：\"这是一个 OpenVLA architecture-specific 的\n      interesting detail，但对 cross-architecture story 无贡献。\"\n      在 8 页限制下，worst tier 建议移到 appendix。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      Framework reframe 下可保留为 appendix 的 \"framework depth demo\"——\n      展示 framework 能做 sub-encoder-level 分析。但不占 main text 篇幅。\n\n  - name: \"Cross-Architecture R² Exit Collapse Matrix\"\n    plan_id: \"cross_arch_r2_matrix\"\n    description: \"3 架构 × 4 suite 的 R² exit collapse 矩阵——D095 升级的核心证据\"\n    expected_results:\n      total_matrix_cells: 10\n      cells_with_clear_collapse: 6\n      cells_with_weak_or_absent_collapse: 4\n      openvla_goal_trained_delta: 0.069\n      openvla_spatial_trained_delta: 0.04\n      openvla_object_trained_delta: 0.121\n      openvla_long_trained_delta: 0.004\n      tracvla_goal_trained_delta: 0.09\n      tracvla_spatial_trained_delta: 0.138\n      tracvla_object_trained_delta: 0.294\n      tracvla_long_trained_delta: 0.198\n      nora_goal_trained_delta: 0.691\n      nora_spatial_trained_delta: 0.302\n      mean_trained_exit_delta: 0.096\n      cross_arch_r2_peak_layer_std: 6.2\n      r2_collapse_confirmed_cells: 6\n    result_rationale: >\n      Worst tier 假设：(1) OpenVLA Spatial（RUNNING）结果弱——exit delta 仅 0.04，\n      远低于其他 cells，且 untrained 也有 0.023 delta，training effect 仅 1.7x。\n      (2) OpenVLA Long (OFT) delta=0.004 已是 outlier。(3) NORA Object/Long 缺失（无\n      checkpoint），矩阵只有 10/12 cells。(4) 6/10 cells 有 clear collapse（delta>0.10\n      且 trained>>untrained），但 4 cells 弱或例外。\n\n      Reviewer 攻击：\"你们声称 'architecture-independent' 但 10 个 cell 中 4 个\n      不支持。OpenVLA 的 2/4 suites 要么 delta≈0 (Long) 要么 delta 很小 (Spatial)。\n      只有 TracVLA 和 NORA 显示强 collapse——但这两个是你们自己训练的 checkpoint\n      而非社区标准模型。OpenVLA 是唯一的社区 checkpoint，它的结果最弱。\n      这可能说明 strong exit collapse 是你们训练流程的 artifact 而非\n      VLA training 的 inherent property。\"\n\n      Reviewer B 补充：\"NORA goal delta=0.691 和 spatial delta=0.302 是极端值——\n      比其他架构高一个数量级。这种 high variance across architectures（std=6.2\n      in peak layer）说明 exit collapse 的 magnitude 高度 architecture-dependent，\n      而你们只是 cherry-pick 了所有 delta>0 的 cell 来 claim 'consistent'。\n      Consistent direction（都 >0）但 inconsistent magnitude（0.004 到 0.691）\n      ——这不叫 architecture-independent signature，这叫 noisy observation。\"\n    tables:\n      - title: \"R² Exit Collapse Matrix (Worst-Tier Interpretation)\"\n        columns: [\"Architecture\", \"Suite\", \"Trained Delta\", \"Untrained Delta\", \"Ratio\", \"Verdict\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"OpenVLA\", \"Goal\", \"0.069\", \"0.015\", \"4.6x\", \"Moderate\"]\n          - [\"OpenVLA\", \"Spatial\", \"0.040\", \"0.023\", \"1.7x\", \"Weak — near noise\"]\n          - [\"OpenVLA\", \"Object\", \"0.121\", \"0.076\", \"1.6x\", \"Moderate but untrained also high\"]\n          - [\"OpenVLA\", \"Long (OFT)\", \"0.004\", \"0.016\", \"0.25x\", \"FAIL — no collapse\"]\n          - [\"TracVLA\", \"Goal\", \"0.090\", \"0.048\", \"1.9x\", \"Weak\"]\n          - [\"TracVLA\", \"Spatial\", \"0.138\", \"0.016\", \"8.6x\", \"Strong\"]\n          - [\"TracVLA\", \"Object\", \"0.294\", \"0.009\", \"32.7x\", \"Strong\"]\n          - [\"TracVLA\", \"Long\", \"0.198\", \"0.028\", \"7.1x\", \"Strong\"]\n          - [\"NORA\", \"Goal\", \"0.691\", \"0.044\", \"15.7x\", \"Extreme — outlier?\"]\n          - [\"NORA\", \"Spatial\", \"0.302\", \"0.037\", \"8.2x\", \"Strong\"]\n      - title: \"Matrix Coverage and Gaps\"\n        columns: [\"Metric\", \"Value\", \"Worst Interpretation\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Cells filled\", \"10/12\", \"NORA Object/Long missing — incomplete\"]\n          - [\"Clear collapse (>0.10)\", \"6/10\", \"Only 60% cells show clear effect\"]\n          - [\"Weak/absent\", \"4/10\", \"40% cells ambiguous or failed\"]\n          - [\"Delta range\", \"0.004–0.691\", \"172x range — not 'consistent'\"]\n          - [\"Peak layer std\", \"6.2\", \"High variability in where collapse occurs\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Heatmap: 3×4 matrix 用 color intensity 表示 delta magnitude，4 cells 用虚线边框标注 'weak/absent'，2 cells 灰色标注 'missing'\"\n      - \"Box plot: delta distribution across 10 cells，标注 median=0.096 和 IQR 显示 high spread\"\n    analysis: >\n      Worst tier 核心判定：cross-architecture R² exit collapse 是方向一致的（9/10 trained>untrained）\n      但 magnitude 高度不一致（0.004-0.691）。\"Architecture-independent signature\" claim\n      在 worst tier 下被降级为 \"a directionally consistent but magnitude-variable observation\"。\n      Reviewer 要求：(1) 解释 magnitude variation 的 mechanism（为什么 NORA 15x 于 OpenVLA？），\n      (2) 排除 training procedure confound（自训练 vs 社区 checkpoint），\n      (3) 提供 NLP fine-tuning baseline 排除 decoder-only generic effect。\n      Framework reframe：exit collapse 降为 \"one of the patterns detected by our framework\"\n      而非 \"the architecture-independent signature\"。强调 framework 能 systematically\n      reveal cross-architecture variation 而非 uniformity。\n\n  - name: \"Cross-Architecture L1 Attention (D090 Training-Induced vs Base-Model)\"\n    plan_id: \"cross_arch_l1_attention\"\n    description: \"3 架构的 L1 instruction-dominant heads 对比——D090 区分 training vs base-model effects\"\n    expected_results:\n      openvla_trained_l1_heads: 24\n      openvla_untrained_l1_heads: 0\n      openvla_oxe_l1_heads: 25\n      tracvla_trained_l1_heads: [27, 30]\n      tracvla_untrained_l1_heads: 32\n      nora_trained_l1_heads: [12, 13]\n      nora_untrained_l1_heads: [13, 14]\n      training_induced: false\n      base_model_dependent: true\n    result_rationale: >\n      D090 发现 L1 head count 是 base-model-dependent 而非 training-induced。\n      Worst tier 解读：这是论文最严重的自我削弱。Reviewer：\"你们自己证明了\n      L1 routing——论文最 visually striking 的结果（0→9→24 heads gradient）——\n      不是训练学到的。TracVLA untrained 已经 32/32 全极化，NORA untrained 已经\n      13/16。那 VLA training 到底贡献了什么？剩下的 training-induced effects\n      只有 R² exit collapse 和 CF sensitivity。但 exit collapse 可能是 generic\n      fine-tuning effect（见上），CF sensitivity 可能只是 'model produces\n      different outputs for different inputs' 的 trivial restatement。\n      你们把自己的 contribution 证伪到只剩一个 questionable finding。\"\n\n      D090 被解读为 \"VLA training 的独特效果只剩 exit collapse 一个，contribution 太薄\"。\n      即使 exit collapse confirmed in 6/10 cells，作为唯一 training-induced effect\n      支撑一篇 CoRL paper 太单薄。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"L1 Heads: Base-Model Dominance (D090)\"\n        columns: [\"Architecture\", \"Backbone\", \"Trained\", \"Untrained\", \"Training Effect\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"OpenVLA\", \"Llama-2-7B\", \"24/32\", \"0/32 (random)\", \"Artifact: random init has no LM ability\"]\n          - [\"OpenVLA\", \"OXE-pretrained\", \"24/32\", \"25/32 (OXE)\", \"Zero: OXE already saturated\"]\n          - [\"TracVLA\", \"Phi-3-mini\", \"27-30/32\", \"32/32 (VLM)\", \"Negative: training reduces heads\"]\n          - [\"NORA\", \"Qwen2.5-VL-3B\", \"12-13/16\", \"13-14/16\", \"Zero: same before and after\"]\n      - title: \"Remaining Training-Induced Effects After D090\"\n        columns: [\"Effect\", \"Evidence Strength\", \"VLA-Specificity\", \"Contribution Weight\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"R² exit collapse\", \"6/10 cells\", \"Questionable (need NLP control)\", \"Thin\"]\n          - [\"CF sensitivity\", \"11/12 settings\", \"Moderate (empty ≠ original)\", \"Thin\"]\n          - [\"L1 head count\", \"REMOVED by D090\", \"Base-model artifact\", \"Zero\"]\n          - [\"Total remaining\", \"—\", \"—\", \"Near-minimal for CoRL\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Before/After D090 contribution diagram: 三个 pillars 砍掉一个，剩两个标注 'questionable'\"\n    analysis: >\n      D090 在 worst tier 下是论文最大的 self-inflicted wound。Framework reframe\n      的关键 pivot：把 D090 从 \"limitation that weakens the paper\" 转为\n      \"framework's key analytical capability\"——\"our framework can distinguish\n      training-induced from pre-existing properties, which is crucial for\n      understanding what VLA training actually does.\" 这种 reframe 让 D090\n      变成 framework 的 selling point 而非 paper 的 weakness。但 reviewer\n      可能看穿这个 rhetorical move。\n\n  - name: \"Cross-Architecture Counterfactual Sensitivity\"\n    plan_id: \"cross_arch_cf\"\n    description: \"3 架构的 counterfactual instruction sensitivity 对比\"\n    expected_results:\n      openvla_object_d: 1.21\n      tracvla_goal_d: 1.52\n      tracvla_spatial_d: 1.33\n      tracvla_object_d: 1.21\n      tracvla_long_d: 1.47\n      nora_goal_cos_saturated: 1.0\n      cf_sensitivity_ratio_range: [2, 8]\n      empty_always_top: \"11/12 settings\"\n      openvla_long_anomaly: \"shuffled > empty\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      CF sensitivity 是仅存的两个 training-induced effects 之一（D090 后）。\n      Worst tier 攻击：Reviewer：\"counterfactual sensitivity 只是说 'trained model\n      produces different outputs for different instructions'——这是 ANY trained\n      language model 的 basic capability，不是 VLA-specific routing。你们的\n      untrained model 是 random init（OpenVLA）或 base VLM without action head（TracVLA/NORA），\n      当然 CF sensitivity 低——它们根本不是 functional models。这不是 fair comparison。\n      一个 fair comparison 是 Llama-2 fine-tuned on NLP 的 counterfactual sensitivity——\n      如果它也显示类似 pattern，那 CF sensitivity 是 instruction following 的\n      generic property 而非 VLA routing。\"\n\n      NORA 的 cosine distance = 1.0（saturated）也有问题——这可能是 numerical artifact\n      而非 genuine effect（Qwen2.5-VL 的 exit layer 表征可能在不同 instruction 下\n      彻底 orthogonal 由于某种 architectural reason，而非 VLA training effect）。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"CF Sensitivity: Trained vs Untrained (Worst Interpretation)\"\n        columns: [\"Architecture\", \"Suite\", \"Trained d\", \"Untrained (cos)\", \"Ratio\", \"Reviewer Critique\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"OpenVLA\", \"Object\", \"1.21\", \"0.569\", \"2.1x\", \"Moderate, within generic fine-tuning range\"]\n          - [\"TracVLA\", \"Goal\", \"1.52\", \"0.153\", \"9.9x\", \"Strong but unfair: untrained=VLM base\"]\n          - [\"TracVLA\", \"Spatial\", \"1.33\", \"0.180\", \"7.4x\", \"Same unfair comparison\"]\n          - [\"TracVLA\", \"Object\", \"1.21\", \"0.185\", \"6.5x\", \"Same unfair comparison\"]\n          - [\"TracVLA\", \"Long\", \"1.47\", \"0.173\", \"8.5x\", \"Same unfair comparison\"]\n          - [\"NORA\", \"Goal\", \"saturated (1.0)\", \"0.081\", \"12.3x\", \"Numerical artifact? exit layer orthogonal\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Paired bar chart 标注 'unfair baseline' 在 untrained bars 上\"\n    analysis: >\n      CF sensitivity 在 worst tier 下保持 directionally valid 但\n      fair comparison 被质疑。关键缺失控制：NLP-finetuned LLM 的 CF sensitivity。\n      Framework reframe：CF analysis 降为 \"framework capability demonstration\"，\n      future work 建议跨 domain（NLP/vision/robotics）对比 CF sensitivity。\n\n  - name: \"Three-Tier Routing Gradient (D094)\"\n    plan_id: \"three_tier_gradient\"\n    description: \"VLM base → OXE-pretrained VLA → task-finetuned VLA 三层级路由梯度\"\n    expected_results:\n      tier1_l1_heads: [0, 32]\n      tier1_cf_sensitivity: \"<0.2\"\n      tier1_exit_collapse: false\n      tier2_l1_heads: 25\n      tier2_cf_d: 1.048\n      tier2_exit_collapse: false\n      tier3_exit_collapse: true\n      tier3_cf_d: [1.2, 1.5]\n      gradient_narrative: \"routing emerges at VLM→VLA, reshapes at general→specific\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      三层级梯度被驳为 post-hoc narrative。Worst tier 核心问题：Tier-2 只有一个\n      数据点（OpenVLA OXE-pretrained）。Reviewer：\"你们的 three-tier gradient\n      有 multiple Tier-1 数据点（TracVLA Phi-3-Vision, NORA Qwen2.5-VL）和\n      multiple Tier-3 数据点（3 arch × 4 suites），但 Tier-2 只有 ONE 数据点\n      （openvla-7b OXE pretrained）。Three-tier gradient 需要 at least 3\n      intermediate points 才能建立 gradient 而非 step function。你实际上只有\n      step function：VLM (no routing) → VLA (routing)。'Gradient' 这个词\n      暗示 continuous variation，但你只有 binary transition + 1 intermediate。\"\n\n      更致命的是 Tier-2 的 L1 heads（25/32）几乎与 Tier-3（24/32）相同——\n      D090 已经证明 L1 heads 是 base-model-dependent。所以 Tier-2→Tier-3\n      transition 的 routing 变化主要体现在 exit collapse（有/无）和\n      CF pattern（general/task-specific）——但这些效应量很小且可能是\n      generic fine-tuning effect。\n\n      三层级叙事的第三个问题：没有第四层（如 multi-task→single-task fine-tuning）\n      来验证 gradient 是 monotonic 的。如果 further specialization 反而\n      reduces routing（如 libero_finetuned 数据中 L31 exit engagement 18→0），\n      那 gradient narrative 不成立——routing 不是 monotonically increasing\n      with specialization。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Three-Tier Gradient: Data Sparsity (Worst-Tier)\"\n        columns: [\"Tier\", \"Description\", \"N data points\", \"Evidence\", \"Reviewer Critique\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Tier 1: VLM base\", \"No action training\", \"3 (Phi-3, Qwen2.5, random)\", \"No collapse, low CF\", \"Adequate N\"]\n          - [\"Tier 2: OXE-pretrained\", \"General action training\", \"1 (openvla-7b ONLY)\", \"No collapse, strong CF, strong L1\", \"N=1, cannot establish gradient\"]\n          - [\"Tier 3: Task-finetuned\", \"Task-specific training\", \"~10 (3 arch × 4 suites)\", \"Collapse + task CF\", \"Adequate N\"]\n          - [\"Verdict\", \"—\", \"—\", \"—\", \"Step function, not gradient\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Gradient diagram 中 Tier-2 标注 'N=1' 并用虚线连接，质疑 gradient claim\"\n    analysis: >\n      Worst tier 下三层级梯度必须移除或降为 \"preliminary observation\"。\n      Framework reframe：不 claim gradient，改为 \"framework enables comparison\n      across training stages\"——展示 framework 能分析不同训练阶段，\n      但不 claim 发现了 systematic gradient。Future work 建议收集更多\n      Tier-2 数据点（不同的 OXE-pretrained checkpoints、不同的 pretraining\n      datasets）来测试 gradient hypothesis。\n\n  - name: \"OpenVLA Goal Standardized Pipeline (RUNNING)\"\n    plan_id: \"openvla_goal_standardized_v1\"\n    description: \"OpenVLA LIBERO-Goal 标准化全流程——统一方法和指标的 re-run\"\n    expected_results:\n      r2_exit_collapse_delta: 0.07\n      l1_instruction_dominant: 24\n      cf_empty_d: 0.98\n      cf_sensitivity_ratio: 3.5\n      cross_instruction_accuracy: 1.0\n      rsa_peak_layer: 12\n    result_rationale: >\n      RUNNING 实验。Worst tier 预测：结果与已有 OpenVLA Goal 数据基本一致\n      （exit delta≈0.07, L1 heads≈24），因为使用相同 checkpoint。\n      但 standardized pipeline 可能暴露之前分散实验的 inconsistency——\n      例如不同实验使用了略微不同的 hyperparameters（probe architecture,\n      learning rate, seed）导致数字不完全 match。Reviewer 会注意到\n      \"为什么你需要 re-run standardized pipeline？之前的数字不可靠吗？\"\n      这暗示之前的 ad-hoc 实验流程不够 rigorous。\n      在 worst tier 下，standardized re-run 得到 slightly different numbers\n      (e.g., exit delta 0.07 vs 之前的 0.069) 会被解读为 \"results are\n      hyperparameter-sensitive\"。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Standardized vs Original: Consistency Check\"\n        columns: [\"Metric\", \"Original\", \"Standardized\", \"Delta\", \"Concern\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"R² exit delta\", \"0.069\", \"0.070\", \"+0.001\", \"Consistent but trivial\"]\n          - [\"L1 instr-dom heads\", \"24/32\", \"24/32\", \"0\", \"Identical\"]\n          - [\"CF empty d\", \"0.968\", \"0.980\", \"+0.012\", \"Consistent\"]\n          - [\"RSA peak\", \"L12\", \"L12\", \"0\", \"Identical\"]\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      Standardized pipeline 在 worst tier 下的隐含风险：承认之前的实验\n      不够 standardized，可能让 reviewer 质疑所有之前的数字。\n      但如果数字高度一致，也可以作为 robustness evidence。\n      Framework reframe：强调 standardized pipeline 是 framework 的\n      核心贡献之一——\"plug-and-play analysis toolkit\"。\n\n  - name: \"OpenVLA Spatial Standardized Pipeline (RUNNING)\"\n    plan_id: \"openvla_spatial_standardized_v1\"\n    description: \"OpenVLA LIBERO-Spatial 标准化全流程\"\n    expected_results:\n      r2_exit_collapse_delta: 0.04\n      l1_instruction_dominant: 24\n      cf_empty_d: 0.94\n      cf_sensitivity_ratio: 3.0\n      exit_collapse_weak: true\n      matrix_cell_verdict: \"weak — borderline\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      RUNNING 实验，worst tier 核心关注。预测 exit delta 仅 0.04——\n      显著弱于 OpenVLA Object (0.121) 和其他架构。原因：\n      (1) LIBERO-Spatial 的 action 空间以位置 reasoning 为主，\n      exit layer 需要保留更多 spatial information 来输出精确 actions，\n      所以 collapse 较弱。(2) OpenVLA 在 Spatial task 上的 fine-tuning\n      quality 可能较低（Spatial 是最难的 LIBERO suite），\n      训练不充分导致 exit reorganization 不完全。(3) 如果 untrained\n      也有 delta≈0.023，则 training effect ratio 仅 1.7x——\n      在统计上可能 borderline significant。\n\n      这个结果直接影响 matrix 的 story：OpenVLA 的 4 个 suite 中\n      2 个（Spatial 0.04, Long 0.004）weak/absent，只有 Object (0.121)\n      和 Goal (0.07) moderate。社区标准 checkpoint 的 2/4 suites\n      不支持 exit collapse = 严重的 generalizability concern。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"OpenVLA Cross-Suite Exit Collapse (Worst-Tier)\"\n        columns: [\"Suite\", \"Trained Delta\", \"Verdict\", \"Paper Implication\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Goal\", \"0.070\", \"Moderate\", \"Supports claim with caveats\"]\n          - [\"Spatial\", \"0.040\", \"Weak\", \"Borderline — weakens universality\"]\n          - [\"Object\", \"0.121\", \"Moderate-Strong\", \"Best OpenVLA cell\"]\n          - [\"Long (OFT)\", \"0.004\", \"Absent\", \"Outlier — OFT confound\"]\n          - [\"Overall\", \"mean=0.059\", \"Weak-Moderate\", \"OpenVLA is the WEAKEST architecture\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"OpenVLA 4-suite exit collapse bar chart 标注 'community checkpoint' 并与 TracVLA/NORA 对比——OpenVLA consistently lowest\"\n    analysis: >\n      OpenVLA Spatial 弱结果是 worst tier 最关键的预测。如果确认，\n      论文面临 \"社区 checkpoint 最弱\" 的尴尬叙事——reviewer 会问\n      \"如果你们用社区标准 checkpoint 复现你们的发现，效果最弱，\n      这是否说明 strong exit collapse 是你们自训练流程的 artifact？\"\n      Framework reframe 可以 acknowledge OpenVLA 作为 \"weaker case\"\n      并 argue \"our framework's value is precisely in revealing such\n      cross-architecture variation\"。\n\n  - name: \"D090 Training-Induced vs Base-Model Distinction Synthesis\"\n    plan_id: \"d090_synthesis\"\n    description: \"综合分析：VLA training 实际贡献了什么——D090 后的 contribution auditing\"\n    expected_results:\n      training_induced_effects: [\"R² exit collapse (6/10 cells)\", \"CF sensitivity (11/12 settings)\"]\n      base_model_effects: [\"L1 head count\", \"deep-layer probe stability\"]\n      removed_from_contribution: [\"L1 routing gradient (0→9→24)\", \"attention reorganization\"]\n      remaining_unique_contribution: \"thin — 1-2 effects, both questionable VLA-specificity\"\n      reviewer_expected_reaction: \"contribution too thin for CoRL\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      D090 移除了最 visually striking 的结果（L1 head gradient）后，\n      论文的 unique contribution audit 在 worst tier 下：\n      (1) R² exit collapse — 6/10 cells 确认但 magnitude 高度可变，\n      可能是 generic fine-tuning effect（缺 NLP control）。\n      (2) CF sensitivity — 11/12 settings trained > untrained，\n      但 unfair baseline（untrained = random init 或 VLM without action head）。\n      (3) 三层级梯度 — N=1 at Tier-2，post-hoc narrative。\n\n      至少 2 个 reviewer 给 reject，原因集中在：\n      - \"What does VLA training ACTUALLY do that's unique? After your own D090\n        analysis, the answer is 'exit collapse' — which may not be VLA-specific.\"\n      - \"Practical value unclear: knowing about exit collapse doesn't help\n        build better VLAs. No behavioral validation, no design implications tested.\"\n      - \"The paper's main strength is the experimental framework, not the findings.\n        But CoRL reviews papers for findings, not frameworks.\"\n\n      Expected reviewer avg score: 3.5 (range 3.0-4.5)\n      Accept probability: 0.10 (range 0.05-0.20)\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Contribution Audit After D090 (Worst-Tier)\"\n        columns: [\"Claimed Contribution\", \"Status Post-D090\", \"VLA-Specific?\", \"Reviewer Verdict\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"L1 routing (0→9→24)\", \"REMOVED — base-model artifact\", \"No\", \"Cannot claim\"]\n          - [\"R² exit collapse\", \"Retained but 4/10 cells weak\", \"Questionable\", \"Need NLP control\"]\n          - [\"CF sensitivity\", \"Retained, 11/12 settings\", \"Questionable\", \"Unfair baseline\"]\n          - [\"Three-tier gradient\", \"N=1 at Tier-2\", \"Thin\", \"Post-hoc narrative\"]\n          - [\"Experimental framework\", \"Intact\", \"Yes\", \"Main contribution in reframe\"]\n          - [\"Metric dissociation (RSA/CKA/R²)\", \"Intact\", \"Yes\", \"Methodological\"]\n      - title: \"Worst-Tier Reviewer Score Prediction\"\n        columns: [\"Reviewer\", \"Score\", \"Main Concern\", \"Accept/Reject\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"R1 (generalizability)\", \"3\", \"40% matrix cells weak; no NLP control; contribution too thin\", \"Reject\"]\n          - [\"R2 (methodology)\", \"5\", \"Framework is solid and reusable; findings secondary but valid\", \"Weak Accept\"]\n          - [\"R3 (practical value)\", \"3\", \"No behavioral validation; no design implications tested; CoRL wants practical\", \"Reject\"]\n          - [\"Mean\", \"3.67\", \"2 reject, 1 weak accept\", \"Likely Reject\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Contribution pyramid: framework at base (strong), exit collapse in middle (questionable), L1 routing crossed out at top\"\n    analysis: >\n      Worst tier 核心结论：D090 的 honest analysis 是 scientifically correct\n      但 strategically devastating。论文自己证明了 3 个原 claim pillars 中\n      1 个是 base-model artifact（L1 routing），另外 2 个（exit collapse, CF）\n      缺少 critical controls。剩余的 unique contribution 太薄支撑 CoRL paper。\n\n      Reframe 路径（accept probability 0.10→0.20 的条件）：\n      (1) C1 升级为主贡献——framework 本身（factorial design + 4 methods + 3 arch validation）\n      是可复用工具，CoRL 有 benchmark/framework paper 先例。\n      (2) R² collapse 和 CF sensitivity 降为 \"findings the framework reveals\"——\n      不 claim VLA-specific，改为 \"training-induced effects observable through our framework\"。\n      (3) D090 repackage 为 \"framework's distinguishing capability\"——\n      能区分 training-induced vs pre-existing 是 framework 的 unique selling point。\n      (4) 增加 2-3 个 additional analyses（per-layer information flow entropy,\n      cross-task representation transfer analysis）增强 framework demonstration value。\n      (5) 三层级梯度移除或降为 1 段 future work。\n      (6) 明确 roadmap：\"framework enables future closed-loop behavioral studies\"。\n      (7) Title 从 \"Architecture-Independent Routing in VLAs\" 改为\n      \"A Systematic Framework for Analyzing Instruction Processing in VLAs\"。\n\n      即使全部执行，worst tier accept probability 仍只 0.05-0.20——\n      因为 CoRL 倾向 \"systems + results\" 而非 \"analysis + framework\"。\n```","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"506abc2d-d23e-45e9-955e-d6d2abc337cb","total_cost_usd":1.1507481,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":67951,"cache_read_input_tokens":136591,"output_tokens":19279,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":67951,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":18895,"cache_read_input_tokens":62853,"cache_creation_input_tokens":16939,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":16939},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":45233,"outputTokens":3614,"cacheReadInputTokens":480446,"cacheCreationInputTokens":51533,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.17576384999999994,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000},"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":4,"outputTokens":19279,"cacheReadInputTokens":136591,"cacheCreationInputTokens":67951,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.9749842499999999,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"c8404669-7376-45f1-970f-e12c54507501"}
